{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T03:47:26.803784Z","id":"78879ad8bab340bd101c631b5d85872ef5a557054b77a99395125d954e003268","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1163},"end":{"line":1190},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"suggested_fix":"Read the reader's open and declined requests for the artifact once per listing and look each thread up in memory.","summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"9f84ff823988f947df00df1444ac281eeea89f73be8a58a561a3a2477bf0b96e","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T03:47:26.804124Z","id":"7c0bc1d4ce6204f14556f192cb2744e1793dddf7901e40fda5fc0d11c7c3788c","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1213},"end":{"line":1257},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"suggested_fix":"Settle the meaning in spec §8.3; count withheld fields instead if the shell or tools need it.","summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"92e1a7c1d514d1f1e7230dbc81b6d87c96715a35d3dab6530c5077cae2e3a3d7","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T05:42:22.074929Z","id":"c0e20ea732c36f2beb41bf6d7e1104b7095cf4575c21c06c5791186ff27a6717","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":984},"end":{"line":1009},"content_hash":"ef0267ee57042e6f58c4b3ab575dbe015b81d840852637892266f23d038afb03"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"a54a3063b96fef31c587959ab0751c1138df8e6cd506a8e53fd98b05edca9e52","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T05:42:22.075275Z","id":"39a1c54356f44fdbcbe7744eaf31ca3005467816b535aad27472cfadbc355512","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1194},"end":{"line":1221},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"78879ad8bab340bd101c631b5d85872ef5a557054b77a99395125d954e003268","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T05:42:22.075594Z","id":"e7e66eb19288f0c2cdb971b056c1cc6fc1d190871931191f3300d32ee3096651","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1244},"end":{"line":1288},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"7c0bc1d4ce6204f14556f192cb2744e1793dddf7901e40fda5fc0d11c7c3788c","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T05:42:22.077053Z","id":"ca992077cf703c92fb7eed626ed6a614f07faa43b9a949ceedb42b46c94e27a8","body":{"detail":"Migration 26 adds the kinds, but nothing makes approval items (spec §9.2) or ended items (spec §14, M25) yet. Their views carry only approval: {request_id} and ended: detail_json, and the shell (web/shell/src/q/inbox-model.ts itemTitle) titles them 'An agent waits for your approval' and '<agent> ended'. The approval card (author, agent, thread, withheld content, four buttons; spec §9.5) and the ended note's text ('clax-claude ended · released 2 threads · withdrew 1 question') need richer views.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":201},"end":{"line":214},"content_hash":"6b150e44f26c19c73d54c553630a8607eb15a8074ddcf81cd54c45013e99d908"},"summary":"approval and ended items render placeholder views until their producers land","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T06:48:40.552885Z","id":"6c780f12e161dad7c4e2dc85d177a86a433ac008d84993d60c3020441accc85c","body":{"detail":"Migration 26 adds the kinds, but nothing makes approval items (spec §9.2) or ended items (spec §14, M25) yet. Their views carry only approval: {request_id} and ended: detail_json, and the shell (web/shell/src/q/inbox-model.ts itemTitle) titles them 'An agent waits for your approval' and '<agent> ended'. The approval card (author, agent, thread, withheld content, four buttons; spec §9.5) and the ended note's text ('clax-claude ended · released 2 threads · withdrew 1 question') need richer views.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":218},"end":{"line":231},"content_hash":"6b150e44f26c19c73d54c553630a8607eb15a8074ddcf81cd54c45013e99d908"},"summary":"approval and ended items render placeholder views until their producers land","supersedes":"ca992077cf703c92fb7eed626ed6a614f07faa43b9a949ceedb42b46c94e27a8","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.109890Z","id":"6bae55d33eb61a855ae7f5a41ba2ca479c32e712382f1b1696be99a4b3847f96","body":{"detail":"api_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":493},"end":{"line":493},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","supersedes":"1e09aa1e3fcacb3e14216e53982ce149b9e74339abed9223145ba1a1e294b980","tags":["people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.110276Z","id":"9119488d0614ec09c5ad27edc06da87d2b8a05bdf358d7cac12a43d5a6660a22","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":936},"end":{"line":936},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"cbc878e00c3498a04d1495adc8cd503452b547123c3b92187b0ad3cc9dad595d","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.112377Z","id":"9862a052b84d69269b0c489938b6ac8807fb15aa89c2d4ddb3c29a3d20bfd25e","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":986},"end":{"line":1011},"content_hash":"ef0267ee57042e6f58c4b3ab575dbe015b81d840852637892266f23d038afb03"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"c0e20ea732c36f2beb41bf6d7e1104b7095cf4575c21c06c5791186ff27a6717","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.113647Z","id":"f5901d5045603d245dcfb54e966bb4e85c71f89234e341040adb04e37a521461","body":{"detail":"Migration 26 adds the ended kind, but nothing makes ended items (spec §14, M25) yet. Their view carries only ended: detail_json, and the shell (web/shell/src/q/inbox-model.ts itemTitle) titles them '<agent> ended'. The ended note's text ('clax-claude ended · released 2 threads · withdrew 1 question') needs a richer view. Approval items render their card (crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs card).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":237},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"39f6bf2aefa0a584f1f8c00198a9e9312b3eb86785a5e5afb8e0d8b0a18b5979"},"summary":"ended items render a placeholder view until session-end cleanup makes them","supersedes":"6c780f12e161dad7c4e2dc85d177a86a433ac008d84993d60c3020441accc85c","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/push.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.114662Z","id":"27cbff0e3033c39396e68ce14a6becee28a49b58bf8f23deb9274be5bb7c1dc4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bba24eb","summary":"The decide and allow routes run feedback::apply on what the decision let through (Store::decide_request / approve_touched return the approver's live sessions holding newly visible rows), which dispatches codex queue: api_approvals::a_decision_pushes_to_the_approvers_codex_session passes, and fails when apply is removed from routes/approvals.rs decide.","supersedes":"8a284a422bdbeef141d25470cf1dc899c1a76e20313674371be797242a932eb4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
