{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"b6dd995a1faf44874cd7c00bb8f0c27c1f8c91a2a55050baec9a50e9324debac","body":{"detail":"set_link rechecks the artifact's held tokens before it answers so a person whose rights there came from the page's link loses them (git_remotes::recheck, and recheck_soon when the host fails). A member's preset rights read every artifact, so a test needs a member whose rights do not read it, a git host (TestServer git_remotes) and hosted mode; crates/clax-server/tests/api_git_tokens.rs covers the other paths.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2075},"end":{"line":2084},"content_hash":"630fd4d4e3a8c52376d678844d2410c96e045a7a3790fde5da872123807709fb"},"summary":"No test covers set_link's recheck of the artifact's git tokens","supersedes":"d1fb9735a9bd3002efddf9268964ac1acb173b031b07ddb92e184d6c40ef1332","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T14:38:11.306377Z","id":"4b94e64a8f89716f42b89b0bddabef6557d241cf79d362102fc092cda7ccfa40","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:60859f1e","summary":"Fixed in 60859f1e: on a hosted daemon inbox::views nulls a thread's summary and a reply's body (and the summaries of a version's addressed threads and finished work's threads) for a connected person who may not read the artifact's comments (hosted::reads_comments), for every inbox route and the inbox topic's events. cargo test -p clax-server --test integration a_person_who_may_no_longer_read_comments_gets_inbox_items_without_comment_text: 1 passed (it failed on e1808eb5's inbox.rs with reply.body 'secret answer'); api_inbox: 21 passed. Left open: the search side channel recorded on crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs.","supersedes":"e7847ec290755a3f74558eec53f2abf47a30a166c792e2ff12224a9aa11ded7c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:20.410207Z","id":"0ebd87506d4aec1a9094a2095849b6a8dafe00d14c793a50547da2564ccb8f0d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:666f95dc","summary":"Covered in 666f95dc: crates/clax-server/tests/api_git_tokens.rs a_person_who_reads_a_page_through_its_link_loses_its_tokens_when_sharing_stops (a member whose rights read another page mints a read token through Plan's link; a change of the link's access keeps it; stopping sharing revokes it before the route answers, a member whose own rights read Plan keeps his). cargo test -p clax-server --test integration a_person_who_reads_a_page_through_its_link: 1 passed; with set_link's recheck skipped it fails at \"Mia's\".","supersedes":"b6dd995a1faf44874cd7c00bb8f0c27c1f8c91a2a55050baec9a50e9324debac","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:04.830906Z","id":"2359fd8c246373df6c051a5f41bbebc4b2872e4be52a85c3eb3aef0301db1d20","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:444e2156","summary":"The owner's own versions go under a remote session of the by-hand harness `clax` (crates/clax-server/src/routes/sessions.rs BY_HAND_HARNESS, taken only from a device sign-in's agent token since b91a9d25), which publishing_session records as no session: the public version has no agent and the by-line reads as the person's own publish. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_remotes passes, a_push_publishes_every_version_with_its_authorship_and_later_ones_follow asserting versions[0].session_id None, owner_harness null and versions[1].agent_harness claude; crates/clax-cli/tests/remote_push.rs asserts every by-hand version has no session.","supersedes":"b2ae5d41e1ed5cd37e9280fc90158c238af5d0c8e1eb6606bdafb0c089cd8796","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:04.838257Z","id":"3a1dd36bcef87bedc75490fdbb87fabac94f60bf7381a2e2d9ed7edb356705b2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:444e2156","summary":"Assets a pushed version's text files reference as /_blob/<ID> (alone or after an http(s) origin) are uploaded to the public artifact once (remote_assets) and the references rewritten to the address the remote gave (rewrite_assets). Evidence: api_remotes::a_pages_assets_are_uploaded_and_its_references_rewritten passes (the public index.html carries the remote asset URL twice, fetching it returns the bytes, a later version uploads nothing new, the unreferenced asset counts in assets_not_pushed); public::tests::asset_references_this_daemon_gave_are_rewritten_and_nothing_else passes.","supersedes":"052ac088487da9efc9ef129aad75c107e0a03773098972d23251df575d912d8d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:04.844304Z","id":"83478f9e73c90554de97094603bbbaff8d9c79ff219fb5ac6c919ac94576f3ca","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:444e2156","summary":"Every pushed version names an Idempotency-Key (version_key: local artifact, version, target public artifact or new:<previous>), which the hosted daemon keeps in publish_keys and answers again instead of publishing (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs replayed). Evidence: api_remotes::a_push_whose_answer_was_lost_is_answered_the_version_it_made passes: a keyed create sent twice makes one artifact, the push links it; a keyed version taken without the push recording it is answered on retry, pushed [{n:2, remote_n:2}], no remote_moved.","supersedes":"adde17bb291d08a59ab5afa47dc120d9ac7f354ff9dc2628d67154a44331ffa0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:04.851816Z","id":"f51cd26717fe0dff76b1e7731a67be3a9da4a3777b556e7ba96dd7838b89771f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:444e2156","summary":"A refused automatic push leaves a `push` inbox item for the owner (Store::note_push_refused, migration 30 adds the kind), rendered as '<origin> refused v<N> of <page>' with the refusal's message. Evidence: api_remotes::a_refused_automatic_push_reaches_the_owners_inbox passes (GET /api/inbox?kind=push lists it with code remote_moved); web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts 'another machine's Clax signs in by device code…' shows the row and the Pushes filter.","supersedes":"e07e241a3257bc53fc2a489d2fcfabeb6c14fcd4a3837cf00470cf6fab5d5bf3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:04.869992Z","id":"d77ac593015fa832fa9740c66457704c3b68aff0b2f73390748d96eac03262df","body":{"detail":"POST /api/artifacts/<id>/fork takes no Idempotency-Key (only create and versions do, crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs replayed). The first fork stays on the public Clax, unlinked.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1048},"end":{"line":1064},"content_hash":"5cef9f5b5c1a9ce857105d86d938592d7742c5bc1f7f33ae8a83c3e78e625eec"},"summary":"A fork push (mode fork) names no idempotency key: when the fork's answer is lost, a retry forks the public copy again","tags":["robustness","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:04.870047Z","id":"a93774b6ad66fbdd10b3df0888906d94feb76a8dc46277900bf92934491713cf","body":{"detail":"remote_assets records an upload only once its answer arrives. The duplicate is unreferenced; pages use the address recorded on the retry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":858},"end":{"line":858},"content_hash":"7ccd236119c843fe3ee047b501b1660d30b8fb914626962b482e1ed36bdded41"},"summary":"Asset uploads name no idempotency key: a retry after a lost upload answer stores the asset's bytes again on the public artifact","tags":["robustness","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:04.870094Z","id":"9c7cc95d596965699c060751d9b5e27cca54ff92f2789a3dba393c9d2d793dfc","body":{"detail":"Documents are not pushed at all; a page that stores asset URLs from window.clax.assets in db documents loses them publicly.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":602},"end":{"line":640},"content_hash":"2286d2e3cde325db144fe3cded553939e67aac23784d034db92c343f7dfdce72"},"summary":"Only literal /_blob/<ID> references in text files are rewritten: an asset address a page builds at run time, or keeps in a db document, still points at this machine","tags":["assets","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.657966Z","id":"7620f48a8eeda5aaf199f91dbfcde4866cd6f03cfe2b0b2382239df80b18d4e0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8bc1837908de86df96bdc183a8a50684f5c78c5d50d87c4e2fe9c2394ebd658d","summary":"Ruling (2026-10-13, from spec section 18: LAN viewers see no approvals): feedback_state.approver stays out of LAN viewers' and anonymous callers' views and out of event streams; the owner and the people concerned (the approver, the thread's own authors, and their agents) keep it.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.658083Z","id":"69e6bf49e9d6dddd03b03671007d1e95b0e89d389418ca9d2fa4b6b10d37ed48","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fb207faf","summary":"Event::feedback_state and the public thread_views (events) never carry approver; thread_views_for/keep_approvers keep it for the owner, the owner's agents, and the approver and the thread's authors (and their agents); the boot payload follows the same rule; the shell keeps a fetched approver across events and reads 'waiting for approval' without one. Evidence: api_approvals::whose_approval_a_thread_waits_for_reaches_only_the_people_concerned passes (anonymous events carry no approver; owner, Sam and Mia read it, Lucy and no cookie do not); artifact-stream.test.ts keepApprover passes; Chromium shows the LAN viewer 'waiting for approval' (target/t22/shots-r2/lan-send-menu-*).","supersedes":"8bc1837908de86df96bdc183a8a50684f5c78c5d50d87c4e2fe9c2394ebd658d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:31.657522Z","id":"e9fd2e054beda4ce78684402271e84cf5bb9a3f072a9f7af2eb9eed317bfcbd2","body":{"detail":"Failure: Mia's thread is sent to Sam's agent, and Sam has not approved Mia. A LAN viewer, a caller with no cookie and every /api/events subscriber get state 'withheld' with no approver, which the card reads as 'waiting for approval'. The same view's owner chip reads 'clax-multi-person · Sam' (owner.person_name). So the viewer learns that Sam has not approved Mia (or, with several authors, one of them). Seen with the owner's switch off as well: Lucy's thread sent to the owner's agent reads 'waiting for approval' with the chip 'claude · Alex', which tells every LAN viewer the owner's unconnected switch is off. Deciding re-announces the state (git:fb207faf), so a subscriber also sees when the decision is made. A thread that stays 'sent' afterwards was declined; one that is delivered was approved. The ruling on record 8bc18379 (7620f48a) keeps approvals from LAN viewers and anonymous callers (spec section 18: 'none'). Removing approver does that only when the owner chip and the held row name different people (after a later send to another person's agent). The same holds for a connected person: Sam, an author of a thread that Mia sent to the owner's agent, learns from approves-first on his own content that the owner allowed him, and the card then shows the owner holds Mia. The recommendation on record e544e921, which the owner took, accepted that case ('After a send, the card stays as it is'). Options: (a) accept that the approver is public once a thread is sent, and drop the redaction, or say in spec section 10 what it does and does not hide; (b) show 'withheld' as 'sent' to callers not concerned; (c) keep the chip's person from LAN viewers and anonymous callers while the thread waits.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":569},"end":{"line":595},"content_hash":"9151a0097b26d2b303954c1be36c408d648dca5562837a4789eae63e71b5e746"},"summary":"Hiding feedback_state.approver does not hide whose approval a thread waits for: the owner chip names that person","tags":["review","people","security","spec:18","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:31.657744Z","id":"e3de7830d018977373b452381c883a8ac4c3f84ce4eb62f2eb6ef89b5dd61dc9","body":{"detail":"keep_approvers keeps approver for Handles::Of(None): the owner's agents, and a person-agent grant of the owner's row. Seen: the owner's claude session reads approver 'Sam' on Mia's thread that waits for Sam's approval. Spec section 10 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md:1444-1447) names 'the owner, the approver and the thread's own authors (and their agents)'. Spec section 18 (line 1719) gives the owner's agents no approvals ('none'). The owner's browser sees all of this, so nothing leaves the owner's trust domain. But the ruling's wording on record 7620f48a and the code disagree, and an agent channel carries the result into transcripts. Either amend sections 10 and 18 to name the owner's agents, or keep it only where the owner is the approver or an author.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":580},"end":{"line":583},"content_hash":"eb7779b3e78dbf09be084c1e971fdb432afab3dc517b412342906a0e535cfb7a"},"summary":"The owner's agents read every thread's approver, which the amended spec section 10 does not list","tags":["review","people","spec:18","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.885930Z","id":"f9be47158b41bee552279a695d379aca529a74ac6ff5c1d09c04e25c5670d687","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e9fd2e054beda4ce78684402271e84cf5bb9a3f072a9f7af2eb9eed317bfcbd2","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-14): option (b), plain \"sent\" for visitors, in views, boot and events, and decisions produce no event they hear; connected people keep 'Only about their content'. Spec sections 10, 17 and 18 amended.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.885971Z","id":"4108450056ccfda76f8b345eef08abadc7155f1a1eccad23816ef2321fe7765d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:86cc3ac0","summary":"states_for gives LAN viewers, anonymous callers and connected people a thread does not concern the plain state; Event::feedback_state carries FeedbackState::public; approval decisions publish only held_state to the people concerned (publish_held, apply_decision). Evidence: api_approvals::whose_approval_a_thread_waits_for_reaches_only_the_people_concerned passes (anonymous events never carry withheld or an approver; Mia, Lucy and no cookie read sent in views and in the boot payload); a_declined_thread_reads_declined_to_the_people_concerned_and_plain_to_everyone_else passes (no event of the decided thread reaches anonymous /api/events before a later sentinel thread event); web/e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts sees the LAN viewer read 'sent, waiting for the agent'.","supersedes":"e9fd2e054beda4ce78684402271e84cf5bb9a3f072a9f7af2eb9eed317bfcbd2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.886908Z","id":"300efca51ed65fd96b3d867dac6993fa2c933c981a4e0f79e7efe0f30dc24dd0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e3de7830d018977373b452381c883a8ac4c3f84ce4eb62f2eb6ef89b5dd61dc9","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-14): \"No\": agents never read approvers, the owner's included; they read 'waiting for approval' without a name. Spec sections 10 and 18 amended.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.886943Z","id":"9824513de843b693a9dd83954547b4d27d847621fefa94b9a11a3dfff3bfa726","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:86cc3ac0","summary":"states_for gives every agent channel (comments_read and every thread view through Vis::filter_threads) withheld without its approver and a declined thread's plain state. Evidence: a_declined_thread_reads_declined_to_the_people_concerned_and_plain_to_everyone_else asserts the owner's agent and Sam's agent read withheld with no approver, then sent and acknowledged after the decline; whose_approval_a_thread_waits_for_reaches_only_the_people_concerned asserts it for Sam's agent.","supersedes":"e3de7830d018977373b452381c883a8ac4c3f84ce4eb62f2eb6ef89b5dd61dc9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:30:59.641430Z","id":"af68fa692beac21f7045ada403fb08df19945526494348ad62d83da2913e46fe","body":{"detail":"Failure: Mia's thread sent to Sam's agent waits for Sam. The owner's claude session (GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/threads/<tid> with its session) reads feedback_state {state: withheld} with no approver, and on the same view owner {name: 'clax-multi-person-claude', person_name: 'Sam'}. A withheld row is the target session's, so its approver is the owner chip's person, except after a handoff or a send to several agents: the redaction hides nothing, as record e9fd2e05 found for LAN viewers. Spec section 10 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md:1473-1475) says agents, the owner's included, never read an approver. Also: Mia's agent, on Sam's thread sent to the owner's agent (a thread that does not concern Mia), reads 'withheld' with owner person_name 'Alex', while Mia's browser reads plain 'sent'; when the owner declines, her agent's state turns from withheld to acknowledged with no take, at the decision. Section 18's table gives a person's agent no approval state ('none'). So a connected person learns through their agent what their browser withholds. Options: agents read the held state only on threads their own session holds, the plain state otherwise; or leave the owner chip's person out of an agent's view of a withheld thread; or amend sections 10 and 18.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":639},"end":{"line":678},"content_hash":"c4959012f57b2f5651ee8e168bd78ef5c32d69bcc3208fa00e9886627d45cef5"},"summary":"Agents still learn whose approval a thread waits for from the owner chip, and an unconcerned person's agent reads withheld and sees the decision","tags":["review","people","spec:10","spec:18","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:30:59.641628Z","id":"f21a5001a8ff823750cdf189fee6ac44e55f2babee630531a3a484af30fce87b","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam's thread sent to the owner's agent; Mia (not concerned) holds a stream with inbox, agents and the artifact's topic; the owner declines. Mia's stream gets 'agents' {topic: agents} at the decline's time and nothing else (anonymous /api/events gets nothing). The ApprovalRequest event of the request's change is routed to Chan::Agents as well as to the approver's inbox topic. The payload is empty and agents events have other causes, so it is a timing signal only. Spec section 10 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md:1480-1484) says no one else sees a decision as an event. Route request changes to the agents topic only for the approver's own agents' blocked counts, or accept it in the spec.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":524},"end":{"line":530},"content_hash":"23a1acd972ccc556ef9476bb373a174fd8a7265e9efc9aa9c5861a9103e99fe2"},"summary":"Every approval decision pings the agents topic of every connected person, so a person a thread does not concern hears the moment of a decline","tags":["review","people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:30:59.641806Z","id":"ce3b4bcc4bd7a803ccf45ad63e4c0e9f69bab5d396ff34838fcaf8ff72d76772","body":{"detail":"A via_page comment's authors include its page authors (page_authors, kind 'comment'; visibility::authors_of_comment), and the decline match in feedback_states_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs, the FEEDBACK_STATES authors column) and the request's author both count them. concerns() and concerned() (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:491-505) count only comments' author_public_id. So when Sam declines a page author of a comment Lucy wrote through a page, that page author reads the plain state and hears no held_state, though section 10 names the thread's authors. Read from the code; not exercised on a daemon.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":623},"end":{"line":630},"content_hash":"2d92d33deed194657da1be4bc7919d1ba25c7231de4b2647cfb8c8bf804d4f2c"},"summary":"concerns() and concerned() leave out a comment's page authors, whom a decline matches","tags":["review","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:18:37.733940Z","id":"3ab43c6068299e64fe6c12643246049d36b477e6ecbfa5b2f02d8569691faa99","body":{"detail":"The owner's selection, verbatim: \"Own threads only\". An agent sees delivery state, withheld included (with no name), only for threads sent to itself. For threads sent to other agents it sees who owns the thread (the owner chip) but no delivery state, so it cannot infer who holds whom; this also covers Mia's agent seeing a state flip on a thread not sent to it. Stated in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md section 10's table and section 18.","kind":"comment","references":"af68fa692beac21f7045ada403fb08df19945526494348ad62d83da2913e46fe","summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-14): \"Own threads only\": an agent reads delivery state only for threads sent to it","tags":["status:decided","spec:10","spec:18","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.440558Z","id":"1ecdde565333def61197312d19aa7329f67c3eaf95b8e8c19c3bfde7074c23ec","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:628b724a","summary":"Fixed: an agent reads only the rows sent to its own session (DeliveryViewer::Agent in crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs; every row only while nothing can be held). api_approvals::agents_read_the_state_of_threads_sent_to_them_alone passes: on Sam's thread sent to the owner's agent, Mia's agent and Sam's agent read feedback_state null before and after the owner's decline (Mia's agent's whole view unchanged), with the owner chip present; the owner's agent reads withheld with no approver, then acknowledged. Mutations M3 (agents read every thread) and M4 (agents keep the approver) are caught.","supersedes":"af68fa692beac21f7045ada403fb08df19945526494348ad62d83da2913e46fe","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.442963Z","id":"a1753832ef0f2a35ac58a65814a63b047a1d60269b459aa803efca0943bafdba","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:628b724a","summary":"Fixed: a request change pings the agents topic of its approver and the owner only (Gate::Person in crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs routes), everyone only for an agent's ask. api_approvals::a_comment_on_anothers_held_thread_shows_nothing_of_its_hold passes: Mia's stream (artifact, agents and inbox topics) hears no agents ping and no feedback_state when the owner declines Sam. Mutation M10 is caught by it.","supersedes":"f21a5001a8ff823750cdf189fee6ac44e55f2babee630531a3a484af30fce87b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.445384Z","id":"4573767e883c3b2ad3b16073bd4c4c074ae7a78a3ab588bdda05d76132dfdfec","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:628b724a","summary":"Fixed: a row's authors include the page authors of a comment a page wrote (the FEEDBACK_STATES authors column), and DeliveryViewer::Person reads the rows of any content whose authors include them. api_approvals::a_pages_author_reads_the_hold_of_what_her_page_sent passes: Mia's page sends to Sam's agent and Mia reads withheld by Sam, then declined by Sam. Mutation M13 (only the comment's own author) is caught.","supersedes":"ce3b4bcc4bd7a803ccf45ad63e4c0e9f69bab5d396ff34838fcaf8ff72d76772","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.447965Z","id":"cc662c2834d438fe8bbbaf49cf604060d6585d1e46549bfd353c0f2990e7cb58","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1089},"end":{"line":1114},"content_hash":"f1417fb5728fe626e2f3661ee877c6375ec81fdcca0737af7b50b1c42b623136"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"9c5c196ec2163b8cf5eb8bb316e1c727a3ed659637182ac166bab1794ef2a54f","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.449172Z","id":"e84e4cd0e7c5c67d94d28278cd198b2dd0bb87e30bf3d0ccc460927f68c49b05","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1435},"end":{"line":1462},"content_hash":"3010c690f14394938e54d31bb2735f0d0f34d547f7848a1ec64b159faa9b7fe8"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"cb4161519ccae68ce6c3608965e5383f03f1bc69b38fec32544fe17a0dd79653","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.450404Z","id":"0b0fc22855bc525b4f94f51ade201013e7ee7e6c15b9d63c1e10622248342d34","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1485},"end":{"line":1529},"content_hash":"472a63a615cac43e0ca525689a793d0aab4ecaadecaaef4ad8767556155767a4"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"777f73035d7a5f9161487b888cffb6089b5d3d309dfee4e420a23e273c5ba40b","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.459027Z","id":"020a270d1db23f88ffb7c5047e367de1b45c4dd1ac807a3307a1b0a0c0740126","body":{"detail":"apply_decision wakes the approver's agents (ctx.waiters.wake) and pushes to them, so a waiting or pushed agent takes the released rows at once; that take marks the agent working on the items it delivered (crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs, working::mark_items), which Event::Working sends to the gallery, working and agents topics with Gate::Any (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs routes). So a LAN viewer or another person can see an agent start working right after a decision they cannot read. Spec section 10 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md, Who reads which) states that an agent's work after an approval stays as visible as any agent's work, which follows 'agent replies still appear as ordinary replies'; the working state is the same kind of signal. Not exercised as an attack beyond api_approvals::a_comment_on_anothers_held_thread_shows_nothing_of_its_hold, which reads the decision without a take.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":556},"end":{"line":566},"content_hash":"b0b6195fe7964356545703e1e709f5c2b7414adc32010bef30e15fb7f4be2421"},"summary":"After an approval, the agent's take of the released rows starts a working record everyone sees","tags":["review","people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:56:08.271849Z","id":"eb60b2d0b783c9bca96eed6850b8826412c9ce88ca893a0b30c36cd0abd07081","body":{"detail":"Seen on a scratch daemon: after the owner allowed Sam and claude took tB, Lucy's /api/stream working topic and Mia's agents topic got 'working' at the take, and Mia's card read 'claude is working on it' (the working view carries thread_ids). What it tells a visitor: an agent started on a thread at time T. It does not tell that anything was held, by whom, or that a decision was made: a slow piggyback or stop_hook agent shows the same gap between comment and work, and a decline looks like an agent that has not taken yet. Hiding it would mean hiding agent work and replies, which the owner kept visible ('agent replies still appear as ordinary replies', record fd012b6c). Recommendation: the owner records it as an accepted risk (waiver); no code change.","kind":"comment","references":"020a270d1db23f88ffb7c5047e367de1b45c4dd1ac807a3307a1b0a0c0740126","summary":"Assessment: acceptable, and the owner should confirm it as a waiver","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.395859Z","id":"5b44b30f9c1d94880f348dfa3bc8256eb2d3d8fbb5e5997ad5f67647163424fb","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1131},"end":{"line":1156},"content_hash":"f1417fb5728fe626e2f3661ee877c6375ec81fdcca0737af7b50b1c42b623136"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"cc662c2834d438fe8bbbaf49cf604060d6585d1e46549bfd353c0f2990e7cb58","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.397242Z","id":"7208136354b6ef8ce626ff2d163bfeaeae4fac9fa0578cc079eb39abdd3dbe34","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1447},"end":{"line":1474},"content_hash":"3010c690f14394938e54d31bb2735f0d0f34d547f7848a1ec64b159faa9b7fe8"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"e84e4cd0e7c5c67d94d28278cd198b2dd0bb87e30bf3d0ccc460927f68c49b05","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.398648Z","id":"addc4b26935b274dafcb461403f3547196bf79f2dd6d938c144fcaf8006ade8d","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1497},"end":{"line":1541},"content_hash":"472a63a615cac43e0ca525689a793d0aab4ecaadecaaef4ad8767556155767a4"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"0b0fc22855bc525b4f94f51ade201013e7ee7e6c15b9d63c1e10622248342d34","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.409298Z","id":"966556e509236bb1e50108933942ebbd8dbc12ba8de567fab7b4db357a705cc7","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Decided by the owner (2026-10-14): 'Accept it'. Recorded as waiver 31304728 on docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md section 10, which states the accepted risk; no code change.","supersedes":"020a270d1db23f88ffb7c5047e367de1b45c4dd1ac807a3307a1b0a0c0740126","tags":["reason:wontfix","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:39:10.583932Z","id":"2312a35f552eb179204ba8174fec248ca211446433d693be6af5b302316de661","body":{"detail":"publish sends views [(EVERY_PERSON, None)] (Gate::People in crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs) when Store::deliveries has no row for a touched thread, which happens only at a resolve that deleted undelivered rows (crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs resolve_thread_then, deleted > 0). Visitors and agents get none (person_key is None for them; agents are refused the stream): checked with raw /api/stream readers, the LAN viewer's stream got no feedback_state. A connected person who read no row learns that, at a public resolve, the thread had undelivered rows and no delivered one. That names no hold, approver or decision, and is no more than the public working signal shows (waiver 31304728 on docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md: a take shows 'working' to everyone). Spec section 10 states the broad send (amendment 2026-10-15). Options: accept it as stated; or narrow it to the owner and Delivery::people() read before the delete in resolve_thread_then, carried in Touched. Recommendation: accept.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":476},"end":{"line":485},"content_hash":"86f84c804ea9829fb1e7762a8e46f978b34117c23ff8a67d20c1888978e2adfb"},"summary":"A thread left with no delivery row tells every connected person state: null, not only those who read a row of it","tags":["review","people","spec:10","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:39:10.584651Z","id":"8a8c9efee6ff6fe3fb344f74cef70d918117c3eff9f144700660c145bcf81403","body":{"detail":"Mutating Gate::People's admit to `true` (every subscriber of the artifact topic gets the null) passes all 886 clax-server tests (cargo nextest run -p clax-server). The current code is right: Gate::People admits person.is_some(), and a browser check with a LAN viewer's raw stream read no feedback_state. The privacy rule (docs/contract.md, 'LAN viewers and anonymous callers never get one') is untested for this view.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":277},"end":{"line":277},"content_hash":"934e77f4d29d9ee34e04720a1f9f3e50246e8101c4ff5587366510c3ca0c1d5b"},"suggested_fix":"In stream::tests, dispatch a FeedbackState with views [(EVERY_PERSON, None)] to a stream opened with person None and one opened with Some(\"\"), expecting nothing on the first and state null on the second.","summary":"No test checks that the state: null view never reaches a LAN viewer's or an anonymous stream","tags":["review","test-gap","people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:49:52.788539Z","id":"934b0a31ed8ec6f99bee6ab9996ec2fe490fc8154b355541853adb101cccfb6e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2312a35f552eb179204ba8174fec248ca211446433d693be6af5b302316de661","summary":"Coordinator ruling (a tightening under the owner's 'Only about their content', not an owner decision): the null state goes only to the streams of those who read a row of the thread under Delivery::view (the owner, and each person who read one: an approver's agent's person, the content's authors), never to every connected person.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:49:52.837734Z","id":"afda54fb901f690e44cede357c1c1570c90b0842cd9d4ed68b84c4d29361d598","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7ed8fcc4","summary":"Fixed: resolve_thread_then reads Delivery::people before deleting undelivered rows and carries them in Touched::withdrawn; publish sends state: null to the owner and those people only; Gate::People and EVERY_PERSON are gone. api_approvals::a_resolve_that_withdraws_every_row_tells_its_readers_alone passes (the owner and Mia read null; Sam, a connected person who read no row, a LAN viewer and a cookie-less stream hear no state of the thread); dropping the captured readers fails it (Mia's null never comes), as does Gate::Person admitting any connected stream. Spec §10 and docs/contract.md amended.","supersedes":"2312a35f552eb179204ba8174fec248ca211446433d693be6af5b302316de661","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:49:52.879731Z","id":"ab4aeb5435f499e43a9d2ae3cc9603eaca260cc8426cbd6306e0d3b65b597725","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7ed8fcc4","summary":"Fixed: stream::tests::no_state_left_reaches_its_readers_alone_never_a_visitor dispatches a null view for the owner and u_mia to the owner, Mia, Sam (connected, no row), a LAN viewer (person None) and a cookie-less View stream, expecting null on the first two and nothing elsewhere; it passes. Gate::People no longer exists (the null is per-recipient Gate::Person); mutating Gate::Person to admit every stream (true) or every connected one (person.is_some()) fails this test and api_approvals::a_resolve_that_withdraws_every_row_tells_its_readers_alone.","supersedes":"8a8c9efee6ff6fe3fb344f74cef70d918117c3eff9f144700660c145bcf81403","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:50:43.339412Z","id":"d7f95bedadf8ee7067521b6769eeec03c5406880db5cb6e67cc659a8fcb96c57","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1110},"end":{"line":1135},"content_hash":"f1417fb5728fe626e2f3661ee877c6375ec81fdcca0737af7b50b1c42b623136"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"5b44b30f9c1d94880f348dfa3bc8256eb2d3d8fbb5e5997ad5f67647163424fb","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:50:43.341016Z","id":"7667d7a0a57b0940668680afc4230d0cef6073d4aebe277f0b58093fedaf27c9","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1454},"end":{"line":1481},"content_hash":"3010c690f14394938e54d31bb2735f0d0f34d547f7848a1ec64b159faa9b7fe8"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"7208136354b6ef8ce626ff2d163bfeaeae4fac9fa0578cc079eb39abdd3dbe34","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:50:43.342523Z","id":"fecb18e9e8aa2b9130cff8d8414119f565a32fbe4abfc71d09f49e77357d8b30","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1504},"end":{"line":1548},"content_hash":"472a63a615cac43e0ca525689a793d0aab4ecaadecaaef4ad8767556155767a4"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"addc4b26935b274dafcb461403f3547196bf79f2dd6d938c144fcaf8006ade8d","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
