{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T12:56:43.417274Z","id":"8d9176db1ff404a1e750ae39c4ca3a6c73adead1a602e21c4c535b45b3b39d7b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:428:430, record 8cee3a29. API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (clax_http::http_cache::compression(), router.rs lines 353, 391, 402); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":437},"end":{"line":439},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:42:09.106563Z","id":"a636dc29099f0bf5828da83e925390bc3df7c81028d32a9a4428b3a8004ec495","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted_github.rs drives the whole flow through a fake GitHub on the native daemon, and the scratch-daemon browser check used the same fake. No Worker e2e (crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs) signs in through the button with GITHUB_OAUTH_BASE and GITHUB_API_BASE pointed at a local fake, so reqwest's wasm32 fetch path for the token exchange and GET /user, and GitHub's real acceptance of the PKCE code_verifier, are first exercised on deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":380},"content_hash":"370e2eb4516a846460088ee54f92160d4a9d836e296c6148f9cb27941ac4ba69"},"summary":"GitHub sign-in has run only natively against a fake GitHub: the Worker's outbound fetch and the real OAuth App are untested","tags":["hosted","github","testing","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:48:06.476779Z","id":"0f8d5ec8c14286acc1cd699cd2c57c16a0c3ea405119f1062d4b11d84cfc4fb8","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a636dc29099f0bf5828da83e925390bc3df7c81028d32a9a4428b3a8004ec495","summary":"Since 8b2caa72, crates/clax-worker/e2e-github.mjs signs in through the button on wrangler dev against a fake GitHub served by the test process (setup owner renamed, a new member who cannot read the owner's artifact, People listing @grace): node e2e-github.mjs --no-build passed all 7 checks. Still unexercised: the real GitHub OAuth App, including its acceptance of the PKCE code_verifier.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:59:09.396042Z","id":"f0868499fb466c638f526316863090447aa6d2d79fe40c01634f9159987e877d","body":{"detail":"Store::share_candidates lists every unrevoked person on the daemon with their name and GitHub login. Handing it to any GitHub member who opens Share on their own artifact would list every other member of the site to strangers, so get_sharing sends it only when the session is the owner's.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2303},"end":{"line":2307},"content_hash":"4b265c9644f1b5d00819c5b12d0aab1fd1baf84eb3528d0649268ee010b608fe"},"summary":"The sharing dialog suggests people to the owner alone; a maker who is not the owner types GitHub logins","tags":["privacy","revisit:members ask to find each other by name","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:59:09.396519Z","id":"94bc3329d6ac9284217b99648d4e12bdc37e855a5aee536044e6191051fd2433","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6a856c88dacacc0cd564edb3fb8debab0f8222517c7a4149c32911b5679c938a","summary":"Per-artifact shares (crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs) have the same gap: a person whose share is removed keeps reading every version whose keyed content address they already saw, though the artifact's routes answer them 404.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:59:09.396759Z","id":"46fb53bba8ade8590aaf2080435f6763a469340ee9c37f93bc4c6bb0e02f6a0c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c9ab20512e515827c65422e29061c4c54e810be2f8e39a232797ebb15228ac5e","summary":"Since hosted invites give their person their own space (crates/clax-server/src/routes/grants.rs create_invite), every invited person and every GitHub member is such a person: an artifact shared with them appears in their gallery on reload, not live.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:57:35.240948Z","id":"7cbff5a29fd12f4dfac8d3267294413f318afe91ea661c4ff5a0902b4b2ab5f4","body":{"detail":"Sync::mirror only adds threads and comments and mirrors status; a full read (every 60 s) never removes a local twin whose public thread is gone, and an up-sent local thread deleted there keeps its link. The local copy then shows a thread the public copy no longer has.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1014},"end":{"line":1014},"content_hash":"0181ba4394d27016de5d1c95870fbc5120d971ce23b757bca2cbab2cb8fdcda0"},"suggested_fix":"On a full read, mark linked threads whose remote_thread_id was not listed as removed there (or delete the mirror when it came from the remote and has no local comments).","summary":"A thread or comment deleted on the public copy stays here: deletions are not mirrored","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:57:35.241134Z","id":"2e82ce7692180ddafe7e4432212c5591f881231c84a5bce2d50722a451f150f2","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-15-linked-threads-design (Transport) describes an MCP session on the hosted /mcp with watch and wait_for_feedback. The hosted MCP tools are thin over the same routes (sessions, watches, GET /api/sessions/<sid>/feedback?tier=wait, threads), which the push client already speaks with the same token, so the sync uses them directly: the same credential, session and long-poll, without an MCP client in the daemon.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":964},"end":{"line":964},"content_hash":"1873036f9d4218f8642bdbcdf4b0c377a4df34ae4343f6a6a5ccd5fee2ea9d06"},"summary":"The sync speaks to the remote's REST routes in a session of its own rather than holding an MCP session on its /mcp","tags":["design","revisit:a remote serves only /mcp to agent tokens","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:57:35.241231Z","id":"9342bba3e743be2dbe643086cc31792365f8e6d7625c115f60b76badec512226","body":{"detail":"The hosted feedback poll's first delivery makes the polling session the thread's owner (store take_in, 'first_delivery'); the public page then reads 'clax-sync is working on it' until a local agent's reply hands the thread on (Sync::as_agent hands it off before replying). Nothing is done there by that session.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":70},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"3030fe931fb29dfbe99de318d74ebb47942d61f7944b51310adf001fd5ce9bad"},"suggested_fix":"A poll tier that delivers without taking, for a sync session, or ending the take when the sync acknowledges the feedback.","summary":"The sync's own session on the remote becomes the owner of a thread sent to it, so the public page shows it working on the thread","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:06:18.492708Z","id":"0d9eb9eaeca0a0360db983b7ce20abdd1d79256ddd8c89d9ae8cd2024f642ecf","body":{"detail":"Sync::mirror calls resolve_thread_touched or reopen_thread, then set_synced_status, each in its own transaction (store calls run on a pool). A scan_linked that runs between them (from any other local write's event) sees t.status != synced_status: for a reopen it queues a 'reopen' row (any reopen qualifies, crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs scan_linked status query) that goes back up as the token's person. A resolve by 'viewer:anonymous' is not queued, so only reopens echo. Harmless on the remote (reopening an open thread) but it is an up-send the owner never made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1130},"end":{"line":1151},"content_hash":"0047cc6c2cc94613381b92acf31b831e0a853ad3bcb7bdc5c298a77a22c6b90a"},"suggested_fix":"Give the store one call that changes the status and synced_status in one transaction (e.g. mirror_status(tid, status)).","summary":"A status mirrored from the remote and its synced_status are written in separate transactions, so a concurrent scan_linked can queue the change back up","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:06:18.492955Z","id":"14f37b684695d54afbd190309f4fc219bc1b94791127c2fcdfe0b03741f01b69","body":{"detail":"drain skips a row only while its artifact has no link on the remote. unsent_of and drop_unsent likewise only list rows with no link. Once `clax push` links the artifact again, the old rows stop being listed as unsent and drain sends them, on threads still marked unlinked (read-only history here).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":598},"end":{"line":603},"content_hash":"98ee75472084959b4cf1a5c06f49c12b19567b7d8bfcf2437fe8cb8cdc4e51de"},"suggested_fix":"Mark rows of an ended link (e.g. stamp them on unlink_remote/remove_remote) and keep them out of drain until the owner retries or drops them.","summary":"Rows left unsent by an unlink are sent after the artifact is pushed to the same remote again, without the owner's confirmation","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T18:33:48.212500Z","id":"a19e7be264ba74aa79f5f94dc80a154b4ac8bcd91a656523ddb8ed01418a2414","body":{"detail":"Sync::ask_there posts to /api/sessions/<sid>/questions in the sync's session (SYNC_NAME, line 89). Sync::agent_client already makes a remote session named as a local agent for agent replies; asking there instead would show the local agent's name on the hosted card and inbox. Since keyed questions are readable from any of the token's sessions (Store::session_or_keyed_question), reading and withdrawing would still work. Not taken: the copy lives as long as its asking session there, and per-agent sessions are ended after each drain.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1211},"end":{"line":1260},"content_hash":"5dfb947c3c26d3c1319dd379a84b8576a9adcb7b5fde6bb39e34321c8e9e530c"},"summary":"A linked question's copy is asked in the sync's own session there, so the hosted card names its asker clax-sync, not the local agent","tags":["linked-threads","revisit:the owner wants the local agent's name on hosted question cards","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T18:33:48.212770Z","id":"34a348acd9e38bd85b208971ebb172f566a21de6207eb5c755e2b21d35549aed","body":{"detail":"When close() refuses the remote's answer (invalid_answer), the pairing is marked done with last_error 'Not answered: …', but LinkedQuestionView shows error only while state is pending or failed, so the card says nothing and the question stays open here while it reads answered there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1160},"end":{"line":1178},"content_hash":"282ef9689b7ca6e01efc899a2efe42df769e8b80b1d05d89da3ac01d35c047ed"},"summary":"A remote answer that does not fit the local questions is dropped with only a log line; the owner is not told","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T18:33:48.212899Z","id":"503a471e7c40c441d99aa65b28f3795760588f37098dd75446e71c08374fefb9","body":{"detail":"Sync::question closes the local question under AuditCtx::DAEMON; question.answer's actor does not say the answer came from the hosted copy. The view's linked.answered_there says it, the journal does not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1146},"end":{"line":1146},"content_hash":"a54581f561d574d1e6edebba11f6b4c05e7c151e49b6d095b14137967c0c7895"},"summary":"An answer or decline from the remote is recorded in the audit journal as system:daemon, not as the remote person","tags":["linked-threads","audit","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T18:33:48.213034Z","id":"c759d6e6d32717c29394d4fe0031ace598e3ebcc9dd648b8c44a3e6b6f08e75d","body":{"detail":"Every copy is asked in the one sync session there, and Store::create_question caps open questions at MAX_OPEN_PER_SESSION (8) per session and MAX_OPEN (100) per person. The 9th open linked question gets limit_reached, which Sync::question marks failed (Retry) until earlier ones close.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1065},"end":{"line":1110},"content_hash":"fed5157b188dec66e1c426d517f195aaec681d6f3ac5116bd3a56d053a428dac"},"summary":"Open copies are capped by the hosted per-session question limit: past 8 open in the sync's session, a copy is refused there and shown not sent","tags":["linked-threads","robustness","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T18:33:48.213150Z","id":"a2013a81406be31fa711e1ad8f500e272f43b149a80c16594cf31cb45f48fbb2","body":{"detail":"Sync::cycle returns Stop::Gone when the remote has no links left, so Sync::question never sends the withdraw; sync.end() withdraws only the copies asked in the current session (session end withdraws its questions). A copy asked before a reconnect lives in an earlier session there until the hosted reaper ends it (REMOTE_SESSION_IDLE_SECS).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1098},"end":{"line":1110},"content_hash":"61bdd84cb5769fdc3705f3fb2b2e444649ddfeee8ab3b704eafb57767dbbe858"},"summary":"Unlinking an artifact's last link ends the task before its open copies are withdrawn: copies asked in an older sync session stay open there until that session is reaped","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T18:45:53.322886Z","id":"615b1db79f10a94ad192a5ba24b75e0e426e330c4c4fb9a61518c597d56efa39","body":{"detail":"When remote_question_id is NULL and attempts > 0, Sync::question resends the creation under its key even though the question is no longer open here, then withdraws the copy. If the lost try never reached the remote, this makes a new question there that the remote's person sees announced on their stream and inbox for the moment before it is withdrawn.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1066},"end":{"line":1095},"content_hash":"6ddc534066bf4ea74f3ddbf0db13f3a1f667bc809fabf5a0e61d859ef7e0ca80"},"suggested_fix":"Accept as is, or look the key up there without creating (a keyed GET) before withdrawing.","summary":"A question closed here after a try whose answer was lost is asked there again only to be withdrawn","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T18:23:57.774206Z","id":"da31ffff387d858a40825784fe6bfcfa9f58b4774ee72999a6e0f8e28f091ddf","body":{"detail":"The link's sync session registers on the hosted daemon under SYNC_NAME. People there see a \"cs\" chip in the people pill, Send buttons reading \"Send to clax-sync\" (and the default Send target is clax-sync), and a local agent's question mirrored there reads as asked by clax-sync with \"Answer clax-sync\". Replies go up in a session named as the local agent, so they read right; questions and the Send target do not. Decide whether the hosted side should name the local agents (or \"<person>'s local agents\") rather than the sync plumbing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":89},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"3030fe931fb29dfbe99de318d74ebb47942d61f7944b51310adf001fd5ce9bad"},"summary":"On a hosted copy, a linked local Clax's agents show as one agent named clax-sync","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T03:24:58.806778Z","id":"6af1b209662e7e1e78e91887987a7ee2acb5d19a36e12c6d83a19395867cebb6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c1df647c","summary":"status:decided: the owner decided the hosted copy names the real local agent with a tag ('claude · via Ada's Clax'), with clax-sync as the fallback only. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_linked::the_public_copy_names_the_local_agent_the_sync_relays_for passes (participants, question view and agent strip carry via; clax-sync once no local agent is live); web/e2e/linked.spec.ts passes, asserting the card, roster and strip names (strip in 576b624c).","supersedes":"da31ffff387d858a40825784fe6bfcfa9f58b4774ee72999a6e0f8e28f091ddf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T03:24:58.818742Z","id":"dbf1ff17e310a4f781e20f17fb9674c625cbd0cca464f804cba9304a730abeef","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c1df647c","summary":"Taken: a local agent's question copy is now asked in a session named as that agent, kept and heartbeating while the copy is open, with one lasting wait per copy (bdb3a36c). Evidence: api_linked::the_public_copy_names_the_local_agent_the_sync_relays_for asserts the hosted question's agent name and via; api_linked passes 15 of 15.","supersedes":"a19e7be264ba74aa79f5f94dc80a154b4ac8bcd91a656523ddb8ed01418a2414","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T19:07:12.529292Z","id":"5a0f7abd5a509bb73169d5a10a270a32af63f3ce8701f0962025b573ed637c80","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6a856c88dacacc0cd564edb3fb8debab0f8222517c7a4149c32911b5679c938a","summary":"A clip's keyed address (/_clip/<aid>/<tid>?k=<key>, clip_key and clip_link) has the same property: an agent that was shown it keeps reading the clip after it loses the right or the clip becomes withheld, until the thread is deleted.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T19:07:12.534653Z","id":"4585fb7a04b04275d65320d5c3f3ddf9fb2139ebc0ebfa9b4171cae7b89fb7c1","body":{"detail":"The keyed address is an HMAC of <aid>/<tid> (clip_key), not a hash of the PNG: a thread's clip is written once and never changes for that (artifact, thread) pair (a move to another artifact makes a new pair, crates/clax-core/src/store/site.rs put_clip), so the address is immutable without reading every clip to hash it for a listing. Clips stay stored once per thread (ContentStore::put_clip). The hosted shell still loads clip_url (GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/threads/<tid>/clip, credentialed, Cache-Control private, max-age=3600); thread views carry clip_link only for agents (VisFor::of in crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs). Pointing the shell's <img> at the keyed address would make one cacheable URL for both, and needs browser verification of the hosted shell.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":565},"end":{"line":591},"content_hash":"25038cf7564a4fa23d644cbec74f4726953b558bacc7797d1c2927a9312f9d6c"},"summary":"Key a clip's address by its content hash, and have the hosted shell load clips from it","tags":["hosted","revisit:hosted shell clip loads show in the time-to-usable budget, or a clip's bytes may change for its thread","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.429535Z","id":"da9f1184385dd1ceaea96e6781b2e793a49955bb7a560773f1f42ae3afdb77af","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1131},"end":{"line":1131},"content_hash":"0084401cde97b2431fc0a50fda577f15da02d5950c956b6bd243c5b7d069ce7d"},"summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"3c0ad45d72addf658c0df8dd111d70dbaeedcbe43ab2437c1aa3a69eeac8e594","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.442532Z","id":"36bf936ee62f6fc3e6d489ce959272c76057960d8282512494305ea39b9bc017","body":{"detail":"is_grant_request includes Bearer cxa_…, and verify_layer admits it wherever a route's need! admits grants, so a script holding an agent token can call the API directly with the same rights its MCP tools have. The prototype (hosted/src/mcp/server.ts) took the token only at /mcp. The rights are identical either way; restricting it to in-process requests from the adapter would need a marker the loopback sets.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"78c6d61d43621b4e72f96b0129c56d3d615b995ec1453af1a1cc7714ddde1a45"},"summary":"An agent token is an agent credential on every route a grant may reach, not only through the MCP adapter","supersedes":"02e4795113e019b3fd20102f7c609dd7d063ed64c9cf714867edb81ebed5dcf9","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.455537Z","id":"ba1e86e09bed38013ef0c38db654618c6d835de8834c48255583cd55a51c9bd4","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1823},"end":{"line":1850},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"2b9834089ab6131eec164addebf62ee1cba97cb83d22bb0b2599974534cb0f15","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.468184Z","id":"b6bcda05a77ae91d87614c8f164b7be01a55f7326e624a43da51e71399ef5c1e","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1705},"end":{"line":1749},"content_hash":"472a63a615cac43e0ca525689a793d0aab4ecaadecaaef4ad8767556155767a4"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"e7b6d312bd2b0f37015aa14891d18ec5fc8f0062b3a4cbe28b0e34be286f781b","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.480701Z","id":"ed323928c4935053b1f9da2de495d7b3c1056843a677badf12edcf3a780f8c97","body":{"detail":"Limits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":197},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"c3d9cee2df2daa7466bec6f2d7785f46a526e8ffaae9cfc54cec9c2e75b2fe50"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","supersedes":"7e78b30ae313437d51c0a6eedb40f1bb60b0f2c0e259812838028c3b789a7584","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.493154Z","id":"16ca7740277688e7d4f9bc59e3cfea0b14bf63263910aad507d1861151cc48b6","body":{"detail":"content_key is an HMAC of <aid>/<n> under the daemon token, as the prototype's commit hash (hosted/src/content.ts) never expired either. A person whose rights narrow, or a guest whose page stops being shared, still reads every version address they were handed (not later versions). A new daemon token changes every key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":542},"end":{"line":544},"content_hash":"cd8d880448cdb31132019e34c90867877b5c99850f7b334415ffebc58c2ce63d"},"suggested_fix":"Mix a per-artifact generation into the key and bump it when the page stops being shared or a person's rights narrow.","summary":"A content key never expires: whoever saw a version's keyed address keeps reading it after losing the right","supersedes":"6a856c88dacacc0cd564edb3fb8debab0f8222517c7a4149c32911b5679c938a","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.505585Z","id":"6b80c3e529b691ba6fa793718747ce500c9f96c026618614e224fc7ca5947441","body":{"detail":"The gate could require /c/<aid>/draft/k/<content key of the base version>/<agent>/<token>/…, so a draft URL is also bound to a key the daemon derives. Not taken: the draft token is already 128 random bits minted per revision (clax_core::drafts::new_token), handed only to people who may read the artifact, and it expires with the revision, which a content key never does; a second key adds a path segment the shell's draftSrc (web/shell/src/view/draft-model.ts) and the artifact host rewrite (crates/clax-server/src/host.rs) would carry for no capability the token lacks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":669},"end":{"line":674},"content_hash":"1784c2024ba3d1b89730649afd8e4da2b8bb437c88275427391e1e49fcc54dd8"},"summary":"Draft URLs keyed by the version's content key as well as the draft token","supersedes":"11916570150370956ef353e1a1bd661c5d34b08c1f6a4e83eceb59211cbe6a9d","tags":["hosted","drafts","revisit:a draft token is logged, persisted or handed to anyone who may not read the artifact","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.518075Z","id":"a625cb63ec4e39e226be9bbdb3c710e635742da1edba4b8b522ea5a0acf7bb61","body":{"detail":"member_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":933},"end":{"line":937},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","supersedes":"08ac048387266cd2bb928126e6b6e4052ebff6d7982d2644f9c29c96fc519543","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.530663Z","id":"bffc5d23187b6379e327f0ce4594308a045cbf4967ef416d844982c5378f6861","body":{"detail":"member_gate drops `gallery` from such a person's subscriptions because gallery events (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs routes, project) carry every artifact's titles and thread summaries; their gallery refreshes on load only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1013},"end":{"line":1013},"content_hash":"cc7f883b42e8d834a7aa6a6e9f0ce461e48a8702065827af2cbdbbf741b80e96"},"suggested_fix":"Gate gallery items per subscriber by artifact (a read filter fixed at subscribe time) instead of dropping the topic.","summary":"A person whose rights do not read every artifact gets no gallery stream topic, so their gallery does not update live","supersedes":"c9ab20512e515827c65422e29061c4c54e810be2f8e39a232797ebb15228ac5e","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.543254Z","id":"5d1ab74090e9c92271a337ec65eff228e721db9677f6495adbccbda8a7840f50","body":{"detail":"The prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1181},"end":{"line":1183},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","supersedes":"c58b033348ff00c73f0cc78f0a1bccaae061e4dc2d70cf4e28423185449e7695","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.555739Z","id":"5be58509f9e45ffbe9b0041b948e8d837ad4d7312a57f9477659b0b8e49ae533","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1607},"end":{"line":1615},"content_hash":"7b0b50000594786778769269c90c8b6ed7c453ad2d601bcdc1a9e8dbea8ea63c"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","supersedes":"9bcf0380fb4fa6531995f18637bbb012e2d39efaeb42770983a749870228ffe0","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.568311Z","id":"d484d16de22d2b4c19dda96b82f570feb9c533a244d26629e7f5366be51b72c3","body":{"detail":"Store::share_candidates lists every unrevoked person on the daemon with their name and GitHub login. Handing it to any GitHub member who opens Share on their own artifact would list every other member of the site to strangers, so get_sharing sends it only when the session is the owner's.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2387},"end":{"line":2391},"content_hash":"4b265c9644f1b5d00819c5b12d0aab1fd1baf84eb3528d0649268ee010b608fe"},"summary":"The sharing dialog suggests people to the owner alone; a maker who is not the owner types GitHub logins","supersedes":"f0868499fb466c638f526316863090447aa6d2d79fe40c01634f9159987e877d","tags":["privacy","revisit:members ask to find each other by name","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.581065Z","id":"3f88c0a68442030d3cffc7d313582e458173f91799796b89d691889bb73f0a95","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":654},"end":{"line":661},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"f3b6a1102227229ccdd6cbb9095e18b03042a00cd2abbcf8aa97841a91790a88","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.593641Z","id":"f85b5770b52cca87d0af0f138fecd34f774349f755fba3d23e5bcea609aa4ba0","body":{"detail":"The hosted feedback poll's first delivery makes the polling session the thread's owner (store take_in, 'first_delivery'); the public page then reads 'clax-sync is working on it' until a local agent's reply hands the thread on (Sync::as_agent hands it off before replying). Nothing is done there by that session.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":89},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"3030fe931fb29dfbe99de318d74ebb47942d61f7944b51310adf001fd5ce9bad"},"suggested_fix":"A poll tier that delivers without taking, for a sync session, or ending the take when the sync acknowledges the feedback.","summary":"The sync's own session on the remote becomes the owner of a thread sent to it, so the public page shows it working on the thread","supersedes":"9342bba3e743be2dbe643086cc31792365f8e6d7625c115f60b76badec512226","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.606395Z","id":"8e48060533e4aa3ad7494b24b99a5bb324f13db0d98059ceff883fb0f78bca4c","body":{"detail":"drain skips a row only while its artifact has no link on the remote. unsent_of and drop_unsent likewise only list rows with no link. Once `clax push` links the artifact again, the old rows stop being listed as unsent and drain sends them, on threads still marked unlinked (read-only history here).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":787},"end":{"line":792},"content_hash":"98ee75472084959b4cf1a5c06f49c12b19567b7d8bfcf2437fe8cb8cdc4e51de"},"suggested_fix":"Mark rows of an ended link (e.g. stamp them on unlink_remote/remove_remote) and keep them out of drain until the owner retries or drops them.","summary":"Rows left unsent by an unlink are sent after the artifact is pushed to the same remote again, without the owner's confirmation","supersedes":"14f37b684695d54afbd190309f4fc219bc1b94791127c2fcdfe0b03741f01b69","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.619089Z","id":"daafe62ee0769719244bd2325fc8349d454985a0da24bf0940281217a73b095b","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-15-linked-threads-design (Transport) describes an MCP session on the hosted /mcp with watch and wait_for_feedback. The hosted MCP tools are thin over the same routes (sessions, watches, GET /api/sessions/<sid>/feedback?tier=wait, threads), which the push client already speaks with the same token, so the sync uses them directly: the same credential, session and long-poll, without an MCP client in the daemon.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1498},"end":{"line":1498},"content_hash":"1873036f9d4218f8642bdbcdf4b0c377a4df34ae4343f6a6a5ccd5fee2ea9d06"},"summary":"The sync speaks to the remote's REST routes in a session of its own rather than holding an MCP session on its /mcp","supersedes":"2e82ce7692180ddafe7e4432212c5591f881231c84a5bce2d50722a451f150f2","tags":["design","revisit:a remote serves only /mcp to agent tokens","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.631892Z","id":"2bc29fc9fb59256bc31d190f36664a08b337c31106e9c5159587f14d25c40283","body":{"detail":"Sync::mirror only adds threads and comments and mirrors status; a full read (every 60 s) never removes a local twin whose public thread is gone, and an up-sent local thread deleted there keeps its link. The local copy then shows a thread the public copy no longer has.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1548},"end":{"line":1548},"content_hash":"0181ba4394d27016de5d1c95870fbc5120d971ce23b757bca2cbab2cb8fdcda0"},"suggested_fix":"On a full read, mark linked threads whose remote_thread_id was not listed as removed there (or delete the mirror when it came from the remote and has no local comments).","summary":"A thread or comment deleted on the public copy stays here: deletions are not mirrored","supersedes":"7cbff5a29fd12f4dfac8d3267294413f318afe91ea661c4ff5a0902b4b2ab5f4","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.644693Z","id":"eeb415c373ace0e764b717c368ae35844b7b6026104e736b9cc876adc8ea44b8","body":{"detail":"Sync::cycle returns Stop::Gone when the remote has no links left, so Sync::question never sends the withdraw; sync.end() withdraws only the copies asked in the current session (session end withdraws its questions). A copy asked before a reconnect lives in an earlier session there until the hosted reaper ends it (REMOTE_SESSION_IDLE_SECS).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1286},"end":{"line":1298},"content_hash":"61bdd84cb5769fdc3705f3fb2b2e444649ddfeee8ab3b704eafb57767dbbe858"},"summary":"Unlinking an artifact's last link ends the task before its open copies are withdrawn: copies asked in an older sync session stay open there until that session is reaped","supersedes":"a2013a81406be31fa711e1ad8f500e272f43b149a80c16594cf31cb45f48fbb2","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.657470Z","id":"b56e7a08497db9052d88d82a4eba4bbe95d9011fd25216cedf450d2ac52f132b","body":{"detail":"Sync::mirror calls resolve_thread_touched or reopen_thread, then set_synced_status, each in its own transaction (store calls run on a pool). A scan_linked that runs between them (from any other local write's event) sees t.status != synced_status: for a reopen it queues a 'reopen' row (any reopen qualifies, crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs scan_linked status query) that goes back up as the token's person. A resolve by 'viewer:anonymous' is not queued, so only reopens echo. Harmless on the remote (reopening an open thread) but it is an up-send the owner never made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1647},"end":{"line":1668},"content_hash":"0047cc6c2cc94613381b92acf31b831e0a853ad3bcb7bdc5c298a77a22c6b90a"},"suggested_fix":"Give the store one call that changes the status and synced_status in one transaction (e.g. mirror_status(tid, status)).","summary":"A status mirrored from the remote and its synced_status are written in separate transactions, so a concurrent scan_linked can queue the change back up","supersedes":"0d9eb9eaeca0a0360db983b7ce20abdd1d79256ddd8c89d9ae8cd2024f642ecf","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.669727Z","id":"e317e7c9b05cd2990407fa0fc87c1881588af338d3ac4d19ba70b25e48542bef","body":{"detail":"Sync::question closes the local question under AuditCtx::DAEMON; question.answer's actor does not say the answer came from the hosted copy. The view's linked.answered_there says it, the journal does not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1334},"end":{"line":1334},"content_hash":"a54581f561d574d1e6edebba11f6b4c05e7c151e49b6d095b14137967c0c7895"},"summary":"An answer or decline from the remote is recorded in the audit journal as system:daemon, not as the remote person","supersedes":"503a471e7c40c441d99aa65b28f3795760588f37098dd75446e71c08374fefb9","tags":["linked-threads","audit","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.681925Z","id":"b9c906e0258da3f31bb35b49e256852d36dbe99a924d371af4717cb62902cbf6","body":{"detail":"When close() refuses the remote's answer (invalid_answer), the pairing is marked done with last_error 'Not answered: …', but LinkedQuestionView shows error only while state is pending or failed, so the card says nothing and the question stays open here while it reads answered there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1348},"end":{"line":1366},"content_hash":"282ef9689b7ca6e01efc899a2efe42df769e8b80b1d05d89da3ac01d35c047ed"},"summary":"A remote answer that does not fit the local questions is dropped with only a log line; the owner is not told","supersedes":"34a348acd9e38bd85b208971ebb172f566a21de6207eb5c755e2b21d35549aed","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.694156Z","id":"8b1bc67723976daa86dbca9b226269dd09ffd1e913e0f34ea82c278ff86c347b","body":{"detail":"Documents are not pushed at all; a page that stores asset URLs from window.clax.assets in db documents loses them publicly.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":698},"end":{"line":736},"content_hash":"2286d2e3cde325db144fe3cded553939e67aac23784d034db92c343f7dfdce72"},"summary":"Only literal /_blob/<ID> references in text files are rewritten: an asset address a page builds at run time, or keeps in a db document, still points at this machine","supersedes":"9c7cc95d596965699c060751d9b5e27cca54ff92f2789a3dba393c9d2d793dfc","tags":["assets","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.706289Z","id":"ab85ccf62e890536ec0d46050c7625b71f927828fbf6ccc0c6160b61ba2e0010","body":{"detail":"remote_assets records an upload only once its answer arrives. The duplicate is unreferenced; pages use the address recorded on the retry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":973},"end":{"line":973},"content_hash":"7ccd236119c843fe3ee047b501b1660d30b8fb914626962b482e1ed36bdded41"},"summary":"Asset uploads name no idempotency key: a retry after a lost upload answer stores the asset's bytes again on the public artifact","supersedes":"a93774b6ad66fbdd10b3df0888906d94feb76a8dc46277900bf92934491713cf","tags":["robustness","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.828789Z","id":"dc390190311a4d1779b7256d531fa84f5cdad6746004f63e17a4d1c0c10d4d44","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1402},"end":{"line":1427},"content_hash":"f1417fb5728fe626e2f3661ee877c6375ec81fdcca0737af7b50b1c42b623136"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"d7f95bedadf8ee7067521b6769eeec03c5406880db5cb6e67cc659a8fcb96c57","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/viewer.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.841077Z","id":"dd6eeef9914be0b9b92fcfe02b8792228564845b2f4b38aa6e2c5d985c64c53b","body":{"detail":"A Clax-Grant caller writing a thread or a comment without author_kind agent is attributed to its grant's person (author_public_id, display name), as the token's agents are to the owner. Storing it as an agent comment with its session would show it as the agent's in the shell, but a thread's first comment is a viewer comment (NewThread) and a viewer comment forwards the thread, so the semantics would change. Authorship, which the filter needs, is right either way.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":124},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"83ee2c4a800f2125d8a2bab39db59a095b257bef4fe8d7cf0c04be3b50037d7d"},"summary":"A person's agent's viewer-kind comment is stored as its person's viewer comment, not as an agent comment","supersedes":"51025cde9ef902083fd82e66a81f4c0457fd1e3702dbd81b720fbe5165753978","tags":["revisit:when the shell shows which agent wrote a person's comment","people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.166084Z","id":"7557c714111998438f3d63492e734abfd5c02e1cf14f19f5f0676b786b819982","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted_github.rs drives the whole flow through a fake GitHub on the native daemon, and the scratch-daemon browser check used the same fake. No Worker e2e (crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs) signs in through the button with GITHUB_OAUTH_BASE and GITHUB_API_BASE pointed at a local fake, so reqwest's wasm32 fetch path for the token exchange and GET /user, and GitHub's real acceptance of the PKCE code_verifier, are first exercised on deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":234},"end":{"line":291},"content_hash":"370e2eb4516a846460088ee54f92160d4a9d836e296c6148f9cb27941ac4ba69"},"summary":"GitHub sign-in has run only natively against a fake GitHub: the Worker's outbound fetch and the real OAuth App are untested","supersedes":"a636dc29099f0bf5828da83e925390bc3df7c81028d32a9a4428b3a8004ec495","tags":["hosted","github","testing","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.187094Z","id":"60f876fe46d2e265bd870a78353389937b22e7ba6fe58ebac67eb5c4272051a2","body":{"detail":"Store::share_candidates lists every unrevoked person on the daemon with their name and GitHub login. Handing it to any GitHub member who opens Share on their own artifact would list every other member of the site to strangers, so get_sharing sends it only when the session is the owner's.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":718},"end":{"line":722},"content_hash":"4b265c9644f1b5d00819c5b12d0aab1fd1baf84eb3528d0649268ee010b608fe"},"summary":"The sharing dialog suggests people to the owner alone; a maker who is not the owner types GitHub logins","supersedes":"d484d16de22d2b4c19dda96b82f570feb9c533a244d26629e7f5366be51b72c3","tags":["privacy","revisit:members ask to find each other by name","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.212694Z","id":"1739fcd09a2f5b9ec0ee574d903a442ec19086eee6b5118630e14f64d1319982","body":{"detail":"With rmcp's local feature, serve_directly spawns with tokio::task::spawn_local, which could run inside a LocalSet polled by the Worker's event loop; rmcp's own timeouts would still need tokio's timer, which has no driver there. Not taken: it relies on tokio internals working without a runtime context. The adapter calls the tools' methods directly (they take no RequestContext; rmcp's Peer::new is pub(crate) in rmcp 3.5's service.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":124},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"67ec541010bad6b266922dfa88431aa7b67a7638afae8ff33659215395dca1f4"},"summary":"Drive rmcp's serve_directly on a tokio LocalSet inside the Worker instead of a JSON-RPC adapter","supersedes":"68678ccb28a3d84a67b1393468f94eeb89de50b64e61473b49b1f9182f21723d","tags":["wasm","revisit:rmcp offers a runtime-agnostic stateless handler","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.232045Z","id":"7c8c51dd5adfa2640a5fa5a8fc8e2e638d946f12efe9cf4c0d07cbe69d9597f6","body":{"detail":"The hosted feedback poll's first delivery makes the polling session the thread's owner (store take_in, 'first_delivery'); the public page then reads 'clax-sync is working on it' until a local agent's reply hands the thread on (Sync::as_agent hands it off before replying). Nothing is done there by that session.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":86},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"3030fe931fb29dfbe99de318d74ebb47942d61f7944b51310adf001fd5ce9bad"},"suggested_fix":"A poll tier that delivers without taking, for a sync session, or ending the take when the sync acknowledges the feedback.","summary":"The sync's own session on the remote becomes the owner of a thread sent to it, so the public page shows it working on the thread","supersedes":"f85b5770b52cca87d0af0f138fecd34f774349f755fba3d23e5bcea609aa4ba0","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.252151Z","id":"e36939f042ea50532cc1ff65397325200e49ca22b73e374e088702d13c8efa93","body":{"detail":"drain skips a row only while its artifact has no link on the remote. unsent_of and drop_unsent likewise only list rows with no link. Once `clax push` links the artifact again, the old rows stop being listed as unsent and drain sends them, on threads still marked unlinked (read-only history here).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":674},"end":{"line":679},"content_hash":"98ee75472084959b4cf1a5c06f49c12b19567b7d8bfcf2437fe8cb8cdc4e51de"},"suggested_fix":"Mark rows of an ended link (e.g. stamp them on unlink_remote/remove_remote) and keep them out of drain until the owner retries or drops them.","summary":"Rows left unsent by an unlink are sent after the artifact is pushed to the same remote again, without the owner's confirmation","supersedes":"8e48060533e4aa3ad7494b24b99a5bb324f13db0d98059ceff883fb0f78bca4c","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.270989Z","id":"5b7c1e3f5072d92fce66b65a9150f94322a80bc44bf4b9a0d83d39c3faa816e9","body":{"detail":"Sync::cycle returns Stop::Gone when the remote has no links left, so Sync::question never sends the withdraw; sync.end() withdraws only the copies asked in the current session (session end withdraws its questions). A copy asked before a reconnect lives in an earlier session there until the hosted reaper ends it (REMOTE_SESSION_IDLE_SECS).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1173},"end":{"line":1185},"content_hash":"61bdd84cb5769fdc3705f3fb2b2e444649ddfeee8ab3b704eafb57767dbbe858"},"summary":"Unlinking an artifact's last link ends the task before its open copies are withdrawn: copies asked in an older sync session stay open there until that session is reaped","supersedes":"eeb415c373ace0e764b717c368ae35844b7b6026104e736b9cc876adc8ea44b8","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.289608Z","id":"0f9deb301c6e6a885380d7a4ec29258848fc33d7b489867b49a4f604a36a1034","body":{"detail":"Sync::question closes the local question under AuditCtx::DAEMON; question.answer's actor does not say the answer came from the hosted copy. The view's linked.answered_there says it, the journal does not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1221},"end":{"line":1221},"content_hash":"a54581f561d574d1e6edebba11f6b4c05e7c151e49b6d095b14137967c0c7895"},"summary":"An answer or decline from the remote is recorded in the audit journal as system:daemon, not as the remote person","supersedes":"e317e7c9b05cd2990407fa0fc87c1881588af338d3ac4d19ba70b25e48542bef","tags":["linked-threads","audit","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.308508Z","id":"84f258d26341b6b9a7d6016f6745109eb7351a0391f2985f0d4a9159e397023a","body":{"detail":"When close() refuses the remote's answer (invalid_answer), the pairing is marked done with last_error 'Not answered: …', but LinkedQuestionView shows error only while state is pending or failed, so the card says nothing and the question stays open here while it reads answered there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1235},"end":{"line":1253},"content_hash":"282ef9689b7ca6e01efc899a2efe42df769e8b80b1d05d89da3ac01d35c047ed"},"summary":"A remote answer that does not fit the local questions is dropped with only a log line; the owner is not told","supersedes":"b9c906e0258da3f31bb35b49e256852d36dbe99a924d371af4717cb62902cbf6","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.328429Z","id":"c99bf41d7fadddc96cb7839d6fff47ee113aa257794ef23b1c231e47d58ff4ce","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-15-linked-threads-design (Transport) describes an MCP session on the hosted /mcp with watch and wait_for_feedback. The hosted MCP tools are thin over the same routes (sessions, watches, GET /api/sessions/<sid>/feedback?tier=wait, threads), which the push client already speaks with the same token, so the sync uses them directly: the same credential, session and long-poll, without an MCP client in the daemon.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1385},"end":{"line":1385},"content_hash":"1873036f9d4218f8642bdbcdf4b0c377a4df34ae4343f6a6a5ccd5fee2ea9d06"},"summary":"The sync speaks to the remote's REST routes in a session of its own rather than holding an MCP session on its /mcp","supersedes":"daafe62ee0769719244bd2325fc8349d454985a0da24bf0940281217a73b095b","tags":["design","revisit:a remote serves only /mcp to agent tokens","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.347496Z","id":"4f96da1e3bf318d59c31ade2fa898a62d9f518c6c5d56f06a1dcceb878bafb6d","body":{"detail":"Sync::mirror only adds threads and comments and mirrors status; a full read (every 60 s) never removes a local twin whose public thread is gone, and an up-sent local thread deleted there keeps its link. The local copy then shows a thread the public copy no longer has.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1435},"end":{"line":1435},"content_hash":"0181ba4394d27016de5d1c95870fbc5120d971ce23b757bca2cbab2cb8fdcda0"},"suggested_fix":"On a full read, mark linked threads whose remote_thread_id was not listed as removed there (or delete the mirror when it came from the remote and has no local comments).","summary":"A thread or comment deleted on the public copy stays here: deletions are not mirrored","supersedes":"2bc29fc9fb59256bc31d190f36664a08b337c31106e9c5159587f14d25c40283","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.367325Z","id":"92a34960b17242927de5abba795ae28b1d330a09938cae18c124f8d34824e2e3","body":{"detail":"Sync::mirror calls resolve_thread_touched or reopen_thread, then set_synced_status, each in its own transaction (store calls run on a pool). A scan_linked that runs between them (from any other local write's event) sees t.status != synced_status: for a reopen it queues a 'reopen' row (any reopen qualifies, crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs scan_linked status query) that goes back up as the token's person. A resolve by 'viewer:anonymous' is not queued, so only reopens echo. Harmless on the remote (reopening an open thread) but it is an up-send the owner never made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1534},"end":{"line":1555},"content_hash":"0047cc6c2cc94613381b92acf31b831e0a853ad3bcb7bdc5c298a77a22c6b90a"},"suggested_fix":"Give the store one call that changes the status and synced_status in one transaction (e.g. mirror_status(tid, status)).","summary":"A status mirrored from the remote and its synced_status are written in separate transactions, so a concurrent scan_linked can queue the change back up","supersedes":"b56e7a08497db9052d88d82a4eba4bbe95d9011fd25216cedf450d2ac52f132b","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.386465Z","id":"c6784e4af59c1de1bb68d610e83e02cbf479b45886cd834e95411209b2843dc6","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:428:430, record 8cee3a29. API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (clax_http::http_cache::compression(), router.rs lines 353, 391, 402); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":475},"end":{"line":477},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"8d9176db1ff404a1e750ae39c4ca3a6c73adead1a602e21c4c535b45b3b39d7b","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.671873Z","id":"f4bc239e3d0bf99e580c2d074641fbccfe5e5adf0b64231ef603b415a146657d","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:476-478, record d029b997.\n\nAPI JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db94cb825ed096dfe96b9336cb4c05b6de8","span":{"start":{"line":468},"end":{"line":470},"content_hash":"03461796f42a4caaafb7403f510841b3ef9f0129ed6dfb6f95dd2f2084ce5819"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
