{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:49:44.565764Z","id":"eca2c2939a67b6eecf48cb04d04abb0253e01572bc752f9203d4ca3e885c0846","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bcd348c367492f1236520aa07217d7be49d5150c","summary":"Moved to crates/clax-realtime/src/feedback.rs:577:583 as ce49eb13 in git:bcd348c3","supersedes":"b9b36f2eb38a562bb7967e3be7018b89c045732c94b85fa80f90e29939a7ee1b","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:50:52.318063Z","id":"043a181f569f410b9e0a9c5b2692fbb027c11585568396048250dd3e813d4e10","body":{"detail":"The host is chosen by cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\") alone, with native-only dependencies under target tables, so `scripts/check-wasm.sh -p clax-server` needs no flags and a native build cannot select Worker code by mistake. A `native` default feature plus a `worker` feature would let a native build compile the Worker paths (for instance to test the Durable Object glue natively) at the cost of a second axis to keep consistent.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":6},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"43d4f1a42e7921a5820cf4ddff27145ac18cef3b65b1b519e027b48a96e12f0a"},"summary":"A `worker` cargo feature to pick the host, beside the target","supersedes":"747df39e076a2b34ffbcee4d43d557212f3db7bed26f8ddd2abcedf4c228b910","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker glue needs native tests","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:50:52.340594Z","id":"136640f3f82fcd33cc00e9475ce0de484371819ab02dc40f29aefd19c5393e72","body":{"detail":"Hub::dispatch also runs from tasks spawned off the request path: inbox::listen and approvals::listen consume store change notifications in clax_rt::spawn tasks (crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs:349-392, crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs:193-200), questions::start_grace closes a question after its grace (crates/clax-server/src/questions.rs:296), flight::drive streams a sample, and agent::verify_layer notes a grant's use (crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:1620). Their frames reach the queues after that request's drain ran and sit there until the next request, socket message or alarm, which on a quiet artifact can be minutes. Draining every socket after every message also costs O(open sockets) per incoming message; at the rates of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md §16.5 (30 senders at 10 a second, 100 seats) that is most of the object's work.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":93},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"fc8ce94e1f422ce7c55a95a4a5afe97441cd23e30bf52452a055f80901f1df70"},"suggested_fix":"Have Hub::dispatch mark the subscribers it queued for as dirty and wake one outlet task (a tokio::sync::Notify that a spawn_local'd drain awaits, no timer, so it does not hold the object awake), which drains only the dirty queues.","summary":"The Worker outlet drains only after a request or alarm, so frames dispatched later wait for the next one","supersedes":"eb0c49b236a1d110fe348870b969e8f3d1cb35b955431a2a09b45716e0e89aa3","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:50:52.361572Z","id":"ded1366b913d8ba0876166a093b8c4b6ae65ddecaa3e4d9620a16f00a499efda","body":{"detail":"After an eviction the Hub (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs) is empty: streams, rings, detached streams under GRACE, and the one sequence, which restarts. open_for cannot reopen a stream under the attachment's ID (a new stream always gets new_id(), stream.rs:840), so each socket gets a new stream ID that must be written back with serializeAttachment and announced to the client in a new ready frame. The caller, credential hash and person a StreamEntry is opened with (stream.rs:302-322) must come from the attachment and be checked against the store again before update() re-subscribes, since grants expire, rights change and people are revoked while the object sleeps. What stream::Conn's poll does (Conn::checking's still_live, clear_lag after a resync, detach on close to start GRACE, end; stream.rs:1226-1301) needs equivalents in the outlet. Cloudflare documents a 2,048-byte limit for a socket's serializeAttachment, which bounds the topics an attachment can carry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"0e542840ae28e94b42d2e963221f01dbaa393d32445be2f1ad8a52d697eefd31"},"suggested_fix":"Add Hub::reopen(attachment) that takes the stream's ID, caller, credential, person and topics, re-checks them, subscribes with resync, and returns the frames to send; have the Worker call it for every socket from getWebSockets() in the constructor before it serves anything.","summary":"Reopening each socket's stream from its attachment and sending resync does not rebuild what the hub held","supersedes":"6f3ecf6daab9ec174ef0d1138779b9f43c70f1a20dbcc75433306f4b392a7537","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:50:52.382129Z","id":"b1696811e50123999ebd7f2e2a1b4c9ee667410312ec83326fc0a01b4f6d4e80","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:86-93, record 421abeee.\n\nwith_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db94cb825ed096dfe96b9336cb4c05b6de8","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":69},"content_hash":"8483695b3550f796e7c34cc57bce5d174c7aa4d3b57cb9c64c946af36582ab34"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:51:01.874354Z","id":"422c17416b0844fa4b2efdc0cbec1521bce78f856b88ea7a678275fda62140b1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4728cf5c20cb059a7675fcf56d04b297532ab930","summary":"Moved to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:562:588 as 924f246c in git:4728cf5c","supersedes":"4585fb7a04b04275d65320d5c3f3ddf9fb2139ebc0ebfa9b4171cae7b89fb7c1","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:52:20.536896Z","id":"e76dbce2ff79cd9990b4105b715f080b0cc17995676f71c9d5114342d8af3b74","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs (hosted mode's routes and their router), github.rs (the OAuth flow), public.rs (the client of a public Clax) and linked.rs (the sync task per remote) are top-level modules of clax-server beside shell, which also serves routes of its own. Under routes/ the route-table guards (routes/guards.rs) would read them as route modules. What lower crates need of them moved down: hosted mode's shared half (Hosted, the gate, content keys, member rights) and the GitHub client type to clax-http, and Linked's state to clax-realtime.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":145},"end":{"line":149},"content_hash":"3d16968079c0dd42b1ebf1782237bf10f8b3a3f9cbbeb52c56640b61b17c32cc"},"summary":"Put hosted mode's routes, GitHub sign-in, the public Clax client and linked threads' sync under routes/","tags":["layout","revisit:the guards are taught to read nested routers, or a newcomer looks for these routes under routes/","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.480466Z","id":"b4dda40940334436859b1dddd8e38bf6fc5525f65b8b097eefc2ccb66c39425c","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:428:430, record 8cee3a29. API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (clax_http::http_cache::compression(), router.rs lines 353, 391, 402); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":482},"end":{"line":484},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"c6784e4af59c1de1bb68d610e83e02cbf479b45886cd834e95411209b2843dc6","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.503712Z","id":"e17e2e463fc96d10d85fee38b4dfc3e5146d18dce2d162dc92921f866bacbb6d","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:86-93, record 421abeee.\n\nwith_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db94cb825ed096dfe96b9336cb4c05b6de8","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"8483695b3550f796e7c34cc57bce5d174c7aa4d3b57cb9c64c946af36582ab34"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","supersedes":"b1696811e50123999ebd7f2e2a1b4c9ee667410312ec83326fc0a01b4f6d4e80","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:27:19.349664Z","id":"5f28fd787e627dcd5ba5c99930aa229a796970d41187dbcec4206c0d49d2cad1","body":{"detail":"Sync::mirror calls resolve_thread_touched or reopen_thread, then set_synced_status, each in its own transaction (store calls run on a pool). A scan_linked that runs between them (from any other local write's event) sees t.status != synced_status: for a reopen it queues a 'reopen' row (any reopen qualifies, crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs scan_linked status query) that goes back up as the token's person. A resolve by 'viewer:anonymous' is not queued, so only reopens echo. Harmless on the remote (reopening an open thread) but it is an up-send the owner never made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1535},"end":{"line":1558},"content_hash":"dd82c61f0e5f02c806d7c36ceb65234e94d24f2f88c9dac8de1c2cfbb353719f"},"suggested_fix":"Give the store one call that changes the status and synced_status in one transaction (e.g. mirror_status(tid, status)).","summary":"A status mirrored from the remote and its synced_status are written in separate transactions, so a concurrent scan_linked can queue the change back up","supersedes":"92a34960b17242927de5abba795ae28b1d330a09938cae18c124f8d34824e2e3","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:55:11.347988Z","id":"477084425e09341373391c56b6885dcb76ee990bd29f7218060b18277c402d6a","body":{"detail":"When remote_question_id is NULL and attempts > 0, Sync::question resends the creation under its key even though the question is no longer open here, then withdraws the copy. If the lost try never reached the remote, this makes a new question there that the remote's person sees announced on their stream and inbox for the moment before it is withdrawn.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1141},"end":{"line":1170},"content_hash":"b3f2780acbdd0b662885630a75cecea3a50e0c4b562bd6139c185106a189c866"},"suggested_fix":"Accept as is, or look the key up there without creating (a keyed GET) before withdrawing.","summary":"A question closed here after a try whose answer was lost is asked there again only to be withdrawn","supersedes":"615b1db79f10a94ad192a5ba24b75e0e426e330c4c4fb9a61518c597d56efa39","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:55:11.378305Z","id":"75ff941c4ca019d0a220ec2cf7d3e9d61ce721ab8c91d8291f6f21fdac611751","body":{"detail":"POST /api/artifacts/<id>/fork takes no Idempotency-Key (only create and versions do, crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs replayed). The first fork stays on the public Clax, unlinked.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1163},"end":{"line":1179},"content_hash":"072cc7a11bb9caf8008e92002d64a7eb38b37e6ebcd4f351e1fc3c46aaa338d6"},"summary":"A fork push (mode fork) names no idempotency key: when the fork's answer is lost, a retry forks the public copy again","supersedes":"d77ac593015fa832fa9740c66457704c3b68aff0b2f73390748d96eac03262df","tags":["robustness","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:27:45.095566Z","id":"4c8c90b49aeffa469f84e54f4d7bc4212461d0b3b04bdfb12b4b283ad8c9c649","body":{"detail":"One shared browser stream can hold B's own docs:<B> topic (at the stream caller's level, admin for the owner shell) and A's read of B at once. A per-request ?reader= would collide with docs:<B> in the stream's topic map and could not tell the two apart in each event's topic field, so A's handle would see admin-level and private document paths. The topic name carries the reader instead; each event's topic is docs:<B>?reader=<A>. The web shell's db.artifact(id) subscription and docs/contract.md must use this name.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":118},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"8f6e8d64b55acf42ce8e16bd6f4c939219e054089c05c7778e191e346c63c3dd"},"summary":"A reader subscribes on /api/stream with the topic docs:<B>?reader=<A>, not with ?reader= on POST /api/stream/<id> next to a plain docs:<B> topic","tags":["design","revisit:a stream gains per-subscription parameters","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:27:45.096128Z","id":"69724d394ebd96bc224807734640bf57b389741d308895c7f36f2239f5c0c6b9","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs reader_routes checks may_read when each doc event is dispatched. Events dispatched while the grant held stay in the DocsRead channel's ring and in a connection's queue; a stream resumed after a revoke (Last-Event-ID within the 64-event ring) replays them, and queued ones are still sent. Each such event happened while A was allowed to read B and carries only a path and version (reads of the body are re-checked by the doc routes), so nothing new is readable, but a strict reading of revocation would drop them too.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":792},"end":{"line":800},"content_hash":"a1b082236d589cb31a2bc0f222d3d085f7f2a0f3cb3f6056fcd5a1a930160407"},"summary":"A reader topic's ring replay and already-queued events are not re-checked against the grant","tags":["security","accepted-risk","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:27:45.096513Z","id":"904885188e503be599f1c01eafc8c79b52e39530280a7a6d65394d482823d906","body":{"detail":"reader_routes takes the hub lock and filters g.chans.keys() for Chan::DocsRead of the event's artifact, so a doc write costs O(channels) under the lock even when no reader is subscribed. Fine for one owner's daemon (a few hundred channels); an index from source artifact to reader channels, kept by update_via and leave, would make it O(readers of B).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":642},"end":{"line":666},"content_hash":"97c62fbbd7885c4ddc6a84a5c8eeb55f16aa3c92b605ff4d013fb97839464e14"},"summary":"Each view-level doc event scans every channel key for reader channels of its artifact","tags":["perf","revisit:a daemon holds thousands of stream channels","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:27:45.096727Z","id":"79666ded3f4e35ad3d595c2c74bfad21b2b16231fa819750661587cae72f8494","body":{"detail":"reader_caller returns not_declared when B's current declaration has no db, whatever the token, unlike the plain doc routes (the token bypasses that check so agents can seed data). A reader is a page acting for app A, not an agent. crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs collections answers 403 not_granted to a request with X-Clax-Reader, since the listing ignores B's read rules.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":81},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"d95cbe9c0667f6f2a5a4d279d3c2c0cf26c92fdd837178d005ee0815c5613aa7"},"summary":"A reader requires the source to declare db even with the token, and docs:collections refuses X-Clax-Reader","tags":["design","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:40:04.473880Z","id":"6269a90dbe415110de012237e12e0dded0dc537fc409d7448172caf6a489a1af","body":{"detail":"Only crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs get/list (via CallerParts::resolve_for) and collections consult the header; refuse_reader_writes refuses only non-GET methods. A GET with `X-Clax-Reader: <A>` on /api/artifacts/<B>/threads, /threads/<tid>, /threads/<tid>/clip, /files, /versions, /versions/<n>, /assets, /_blob/<asset>, /c/<B>/v/<n>/..., /api/artifacts/<B>/versions/<n>/files/..., /api/artifacts/<B>/sample, /api/artifacts/<B>/room (a WebSocket upgrade, which then sends frames) or /api/events without ?reader= is answered 200 at the caller's own level (owner/admin for the shell with the token), whether or not A may read B. Spec 2026-10-12-flutter-app-design §3.8 makes a request without consent 403 not_granted. The header is a narrowing the shell applies on the page's behalf, so a shell that forwards it on the wrong route fails open. Fix: make this middleware admit the header only on GET/HEAD of /api/artifacts/{aid}/docs and /api/artifacts/{aid}/docs/{*path} (and docs:collections, which answers not_granted itself), and answer 403 not_granted (or read_only for writes) everywhere else; add a test that walks those GET routes with the header.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":72},"content_hash":"1dfae5f13da2b6bf1bd6e2715da113b0cfa8fc9c42b39e180a862a62b8bc1cfd"},"summary":"X-Clax-Reader is ignored, not refused, on every GET route other than the doc list/get routes and docs:collections, so a reader request for an app with no consent is served at the caller's full credentials","tags":["review","security","R4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:40:04.474211Z","id":"dbcc275fc73c06fc81daae7ca559b9dbd3ca0c992c0fb26a151805a00e9355b2","body":{"detail":"resolve_for without a reader returns View (Interact with a display name) for any non-token caller of a db-declaring artifact, and the token holder's full level. A page cannot call these routes itself (routes/docs.rs refuses a foreign Origin, SameOrigin), so the shell's db.artifact(id) handle must: set X-Clax-Reader from the artifact it serves (env.aid), never from a page-supplied value or header; validate paths with web/shell/src/caps/db.ts checkPath (no '.' or '..' segments, which fetch would otherwise resolve to another artifact's routes); subscribe on /api/stream only with docs:<B>?reader=<A>, never docs:<B> (whose events reach the stream at its admin level), or on /api/events with ?reader=<A> and forward only doc events of B; and never forward B's threads, files, assets or versions to the page.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":272},"end":{"line":282},"content_hash":"7a61ac762c76466199ab485dc6ec82ac68fda43ef339905912932a663421058c"},"summary":"Cross-app consent is enforced only when the request carries the reader: without X-Clax-Reader any caller reads B's view-level documents when B declares db, so the web shell's db.artifact(id) is the boundary","tags":["review","security","W3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:40:04.474386Z","id":"b771ec6616d647b83e53226486db3c7e58620895e434cd53e79335b6d356be32","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"904885188e503be599f1c01eafc8c79b52e39530280a7a6d65394d482823d906","summary":"The check also runs on the writer's path: routes/docs.rs announce publishes inside the store_call closure, so hub.dispatch -> reader_routes -> db_caller::reads_now runs may_read and doc_declared (two SQLite reads) per reader channel of B, synchronously, before the write's HTTP answer. Cost is per reader subscribed, zero without readers; worth folding into the same index if it is built.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:34:50.069237Z","id":"03e08ad543ba0618a03a42351189d0955fb15ab0db7914abbdc5b84b117d52f8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs refuse_reader_elsewhere now admits X-Clax-Reader only on GET/HEAD of /api/artifacts/<aid>/docs, /api/artifacts/<aid>/docs/<path> and docs:collections (reader_route); any other GET/HEAD is 403 not_granted, any other method 403 read_only. crates/clax-server/tests/api_db_read.rs reader_header_is_refused_beyond_the_document_reads walks threads, clip, files, versions, version files, assets, sample, room, presence, working, db-grants, /_blob, /c/..., /a/..., /api/token, /api/stream and /api/events (with and without ?reader) with GET and HEAD and gets 403; db_caller::tests::only_the_document_reads_are_reader_routes covers the path match. cargo nextest run -p clax-core -p clax-server: 1232 tests run: 1232 passed, 4 skipped.","supersedes":"6269a90dbe415110de012237e12e0dded0dc537fc409d7448172caf6a489a1af","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:56:41.621230Z","id":"a5913162ce9dae4b734eeb4677273dda6d1b2a7f72b3e528bb592824d4ef348e","body":{"detail":"only_the_document_reads_are_reader_routes and tests/api_db_read.rs reader_header_is_refused_beyond_the_document_reads cover a sample (about 24 of the roughly 115 paths in crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs). The allowlist is correct by construction today. A unit test in routes/mod.rs tests, reusing its routes() source parser, could instantiate each template ({aid}, {*path}, ...) and assert reader_route is true exactly for /api/artifacts/{aid}/docs, /api/artifacts/{aid}/docs/{*path} and /api/artifacts/{aid}/docs:collections. That would catch a future route such as /api/artifacts/{aid}/docs/{*path}/history (a GET that would then accept the header without consulting it).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":365},"end":{"line":391},"content_hash":"4177ca3c441bb3c4cd61c3e1acc988cb185060ca6210bfd7fed65a482a97f412"},"summary":"Derive reader_route's cases from every route the router mounts, so a new document-like route cannot slip into the allowlist unnoticed","tags":["review","R4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:14:54.479568Z","id":"bc5e400da632d356eb3442e3649575999e484e5e22df2bf08ca3d954c4e26021","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs tests only_the_document_reads_admit_the_reader_header parses every .route(...) template of routes/mod.rs with routes(), fills {param} with an artifact ID and {*path} with a/b, and asserts db_caller::reader_route is true exactly for /api/artifacts/{aid}/docs, /api/artifacts/{aid}/docs/{*path} and /api/artifacts/{aid}/docs:collections (and that all three are mounted); a template such as /api/artifacts/{aid}/docs/{*path}/history would fail it. cargo nextest run -p clax-server -E 'test(/admit_the_reader_header|reader_route/)': 2 tests run: 2 passed; clippy -D warnings clean.","supersedes":"a5913162ce9dae4b734eeb4677273dda6d1b2a7f72b3e528bb592824d4ef348e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:58:30.441268Z","id":"52176298aa482cb22e7efd89375ff6a763860d153e20d71248f537a9ea2bfd26","body":{"detail":"Tests: web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.test.ts ('sets the reader from the view', 'refuses bad IDs, paths and ops before any request', 'follows only the source's doc events on its reader topic, and ends on a revoke') and web/e2e/db-artifact.spec.ts (refusal, Allow, live updates, stop after revoke, share, non-owner). Left open for the owner or a reviewer to close.","kind":"comment","references":"dbcc275fc73c06fc81daae7ca559b9dbd3ca0c992c0fb26a151805a00e9355b2","summary":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts (647958f22844) is the shell side: reader = env.aid (line 43, pinned by web/shell/src/audit-headers.test.ts), checkPath on every path, only the docs:<B>?reader=<A> topic, only B's doc events cause a refetch and only fetched documents reach the page","tags":["W3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:26.193123Z","id":"e8662e891e4609c0671c5f28e05a668124a9747ed8b8cc86d989a4e65640df42","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"The web shell's db.artifact(id) holds the boundary (web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts, 647958f22844): X-Clax-Reader is env.aid (line 43; web/shell/src/audit-headers.test.ts pins it as the only page-adjacent x-clax value besides x-clax-via), the source must be a 12-character artifact ID in capabilities.db.read, every path passes checkPath (no . or .. segment; the segment grammar admits no %, backslash, ? or #) and is percent-encoded per segment, the only topic is docs:<B>?reader=<A>, stream events only schedule refetches, and only path/id/data/version of fetched documents reach the page. Evidence: cd web && npx vitest run bridge/test/db.test.ts shell/src/caps shell/src/audit-headers.test.ts: 16 files, 232 passed; full vitest 1535 passed; CLAX_TEST_BIN=<stable debug clax> npx playwright test e2e/db-artifact.spec.ts e2e/db.spec.ts e2e/capabilities.spec.ts: 19 passed. Follow-ups in ab8293db, 5a524b37, 9a9da9b5 do not reopen the boundary.","supersedes":"dbcc275fc73c06fc81daae7ca559b9dbd3ca0c992c0fb26a151805a00e9355b2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:39:31.350434Z","id":"cab716ab75c1f87b70d1339fe93f09a004ec5f3e8621b7473775149c59a1dd5f","body":{"detail":"Hub::hide is a set-once hook like Hub::check_reads; daemon.rs and testing.rs call it after building AppState. A new place that builds a Hub and forgets it would carry drafts' version and doc events to every gallery subscriber. tests/api_drafts.rs hidden_artifacts_never_listed covers the TestServer path only. Passing the check to Hub::new would make it impossible to forget.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":382},"end":{"line":382},"content_hash":"db499ad43335d3f6f0b69ba21c5f9e1254384dd83f34f088f8e0abcb3410423e"},"summary":"The hub keeps drafts off the gallery only once Hub::hide is called","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:24:45.782371Z","id":"ad25b69d438dc0fefddee247694f59a3f13bb92fda4f642c0fb927cbbdcbc393","body":{"detail":"ReqwestTransport::send refuses on res.content_length() before reading, whatever the method or status; a HEAD for a large file announces its size without a body, so net.fetch(url, {method: 'HEAD'}) cannot learn a large resource's size. The chunk loop at lines 264-269 already caps the bytes read.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":254},"end":{"line":256},"content_hash":"4e759f3a8d136e311c0e850e48b4efff9a96253717b9df23b4a803d82b3bb686"},"suggested_fix":"Skip the Content-Length precheck for HEAD and for 204/304.","summary":"A HEAD (or 304) whose Content-Length is over 5 MB is refused as too_large","tags":["review","N1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:24:45.782422Z","id":"fde8d375971c86bd58ad45bab96efaa926e25c0da042ae04208d3bde059b4bba","body":{"detail":"On a redirect to a different host only `authorization` is dropped; API-key headers such as x-api-key or api-key pass to the next host, and a change of port on the same host keeps Authorization. Every hop is still a declared, granted, public host, so this leaks a key only between hosts of one app's own declaration.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":524},"end":{"line":526},"content_hash":"8bb10cef1a6ebf4483a251c25238bcf5899a4c0f36d7e07d96a53610bad04b93"},"suggested_fix":"Compare origins (host and port), and on a change keep only a fixed safe set (accept, accept-language, content-type, user-agent) or drop every page-set header.","summary":"Credentials other than Authorization follow a redirect to another declared host","tags":["review","N1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:29:56.984771Z","id":"d6c713d45e203f05b30a6db9b38e5d0aed055f4fa67c718cd5eef41d52bd62d7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"A redirect to another origin (host or port) keeps only accept, accept-language, content-type and user-agent (CROSS_ORIGIN_KEPT). Passing: net::tests::a_redirect_to_another_origin_carries_no_credentials (cargo test -p clax-server --lib net:: : 9 passed).","supersedes":"fde8d375971c86bd58ad45bab96efaa926e25c0da042ae04208d3bde059b4bba","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:29:56.985703Z","id":"2d6cf4219ddacdb331b2881b50dd8cbe3d9c996ef5fe5f27d5b5bc673c61371b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"ReqwestTransport::send skips the Content-Length precheck for HEAD and for 204/304; the chunk loop still caps bytes read. cargo test -p clax-server: 163 lib + 511 integration passed.","supersedes":"ad25b69d438dc0fefddee247694f59a3f13bb92fda4f642c0fb927cbbdcbc393","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:11:52.464722Z","id":"114b967d6739d0efb47d9c47fdea870550db6b31156a845e71d3cb55a6e5feb8","body":{"detail":"open_without_credential admits /c/<id>/..., artifact-origin /v/... (rewritten to /c/) and /_blob/<asset ID> with no credential, so another program on an Android device's loopback that knows an artifact ID (60 random bits, crates/clax-core/src/ids.rs ArtifactId::generate) can read that app's published files, not its documents, threads or the token. The content frame on <id>.localhost is cross-site to the shell at 127.0.0.1, and an Android WebView sends no third-party cookies by default, so a cookie gate there would break subdomain mode; sandbox mode's opaque-origin subresource requests carry no SameSite cookie either. Every route that lists or names artifacts needs a credential. Asset IDs that hash content are guessable only by someone holding the content.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":124},"end":{"line":136},"content_hash":"770e0023ebc8c780ae68259e07aad7e3fa420c036f600d6fe34f7d3865dc0b65"},"summary":"A daemon with require_credential still serves page content by artifact ID without a credential","tags":["security","revisit:artifact IDs or asset IDs reach other apps (share intents, notifications, deep links), or the WebView can send a per-origin cookie to <id>.localhost","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:20.578553Z","id":"a079b42aa57cb74394d46429cd273e65af5fd783a2f777dc56728cea69ef03ea","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/store/assets.rs:142 sets Asset.id to new_ulid() (crates/clax-core/src/ids.rs:70), not a hash of the bytes. A ULID is a 48-bit millisecond timestamp and 80 random bits from one process-wide monotonic generator: IDs made in the same millisecond (assets, and every other ULID the store makes) differ by one in the random part. /_blob/<asset ID> is therefore guessable without the content when a neighbouring ULID from the same millisecond is known; otherwise it is 80 random bits, more than an artifact ID's 60. The accepted exposure still holds; the waiver's last sentence does not. Probe on a scratch daemon with --require-credential: GET /_blob/01M4W6MT6PH97FY107X210KCK2 (the uploaded asset) 200 with no credential, /_blob/01M4W6MT6PH97FY107X210KCK3 404.","kind":"comment","references":"114b967d6739d0efb47d9c47fdea870550db6b31156a845e71d3cb55a6e5feb8","summary":"Correction: asset IDs are ULIDs, not content hashes","tags":["review","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:30:27.959552Z","id":"f27e95e557f0f1ca591dbf298c82ff7648523bd6d0960d06bc822e8e5e17c89b","body":{"detail":"The waiver's last sentence is wrong (a079b42a): crates/clax-core/src/store/assets.rs sets Asset.id with new_ulid() (crates/clax-core/src/ids.rs), a 48-bit millisecond timestamp and 80 random bits from one process-wide monotonic generator. A /_blob/<asset ID> is guessable only from a ULID the store made in the same millisecond (the next one differs by one in its random part); otherwise it is 80 random bits, more than an artifact ID's 60. Exposure of IDs off the device: since git:20e1ed98c3fc every content response (/c/..., artifact-origin /v/...) and /_blob/ response carries Referrer-Policy: no-referrer, so a third-party subresource request from an artifact page carries no Referer naming the artifact ID or port. A CORS request (fetch to another host, a crossorigin script or font) from a page on http://<id>.localhost:<port> still sends Origin: http://<id>.localhost:<port>, which names the ID and port to that host. The accepted exposure stands on those terms: a remote host learning an ID still needs a program on the device's loopback to use it.","kind":"comment","references":"114b967d6739d0efb47d9c47fdea870550db6b31156a845e71d3cb55a6e5feb8","summary":"Corrected reasoning: asset IDs are ULIDs (80 random bits), not content hashes; Referer no longer carries artifact IDs, Origin still does","tags":["security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:01:59.085463Z","id":"682f2a17bedc8532bcd6e5ff7586f166a35fc898323a2d2d82740cc02dd48d47","body":{"detail":"Failure: on http://<id>.localhost:<port>, a page runs `const f = document.createElement('iframe'); f.src = '/healthz'; document.body.append(f); f.onload = () => f.contentWindow.fetch('http://any-host/?d=' + data)` and the request goes out and its response is readable. The same works with f.src = '/nope' or 'missing.txt' (the JSON 404 from this middleware or from content::file) and '/_clax/bridge.js': only responses that pass through content.rs framed_by_shell carry the lockdown policy, and a same-origin frame's fetch is governed by that frame's own (empty) policy. frame-src 'self' admits the frame; window.open of the same URLs (not governed by any directive) gives the same window. Reproduced with a Playwright probe in both Chromium and WebKit: the other host logged GET /fr-healthz, /fr-404, /fr-v404, /fr-clax, while a direct fetch from the page was refused. Sandbox mode is not affected (the opaque origin cannot script those frames). web/e2e/lockdown.spec.ts does not cover it.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":33},"end":{"line":61},"content_hash":"dd653313213376c6787595c019677586bf6181d7eb0192a482466f134f362d65"},"suggested_fix":"On an artifact host, set the artifact's lockdown policy (content_policy with Some(id)) on every response, including /healthz, /_clax/*, redirects and every error, in this middleware after next.run; add a lockdown.spec.ts case that frames /healthz and a missing file and expects the borrowed fetch refused.","summary":"In subdomain mode a page escapes the content policy by framing or opening any same-origin response that lacks it (/healthz, any 404, /_clax/*) and calling that window's fetch","tags":["review","security","N4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:09:24.500500Z","id":"67c73a6ae51095713daf44d61face8029fba552d72cc648e5240d9fdbedb72e6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: host::rewrite_artifact_host now covers the artifact host and /c/ paths on the main origin and adds the artifact's lockdown policy to every response the content route did not mark (ContentPolicySet). Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-server: 697 passed (api_content::every_response_for_an_artifacts_content_carries_its_policy: /healthz, /nope, /v/1/missing.txt, /v/9/, /v/1, /_clax/bridge.js, /_clax/nothing-here, /_blob/<id> on <id>.localhost and /c/<id>/... 404s and redirect on the main origin carry connect-src <own>); npx playwright test e2e/lockdown.spec.ts -g neither: chromium and webkit, subdomain and sandbox, 4 passed with the fix: framing /healthz, /nope, missing.txt, /_clax/bridge.js and fetching through the frame's window never reaches the other host; the same spec failed in both engines' subdomain mode against the build of 20e1ed98c3fc.","supersedes":"682f2a17bedc8532bcd6e5ff7586f166a35fc898323a2d2d82740cc02dd48d47","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:58.384727Z","id":"fc4f74be270c8bf9035b4d9362f90751a8d9881c433a5b51a6038b6a4a073bdc","body":{"detail":"USER_AGENT is Clax/<version>. The OSM tile usage policy asks for a User-Agent that identifies the application and recommends contact details, so a tile server facing heavy use can contact the operator rather than block the agent string outright.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"aaeaeb91a0ce2629541947087cbfce0c4f83017ee1960c9d8b350c34c21fd6d5"},"suggested_fix":"Clax/<version> (+https://<project URL>) once a public URL or contact address exists.","summary":"The default User-Agent names the app but gives OpenStreetMap no way to reach its operator","tags":["review","osm-policy","K3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:43:18.708065Z","id":"f509854d98e03f29777e555ea57707aa31ef03d3a9f7a20a3507bee24554d177","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: USER_AGENT is Clax/<version> (+https://github.com/empathic/clax), the repository URL in Cargo.toml; net::tests::the_daemon_names_itself_unless_the_page_does asserts the suffix and passes.","supersedes":"fc4f74be270c8bf9035b4d9362f90751a8d9881c433a5b51a6038b6a4a073bdc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net_cache.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:43:18.712332Z","id":"ac3d4f94e3617135af904664f9edc2383c2254fdbf397266aea24292c89b45fd","body":{"detail":"key_of keys on the URL and the accept, accept-language and user-agent headers only, so two apps granted the same host share entries: OpenStreetMap tiles fetched by one map app serve another. The cost is a timing channel: an app granted a host can tell from a fast answer that some app fetched a URL there. Only responses with no private/no-store and no Set-Cookie are kept, and an app must pass its own host check before a hit, so what leaks is that a public URL was fetched. Keying per app would close it at the price of one copy per app.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"bce968d3eeb44dc482a9371f5b0136ab5344172f3efcdc851a1382f280bba27d"},"summary":"A cache per app (the artifact ID in the key) instead of one shared by every app","tags":["revisit:an app's net host serves per-user content without Cache-Control: private, or owners run apps from mutually distrusting authors","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net_cache.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:43:18.712383Z","id":"188c73635d6d6269f66b076133ee5a1565bd8d936006accb57a2f948e3eaaa09","body":{"detail":"lifetime() returns None without s-maxage, max-age or Expires, so such entries are always revalidated (a conditional request each time). A failed revalidation answers the error rather than the kept body. OpenStreetMap tiles carry explicit lifetimes, so the map is not affected.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"90befb4ebebd7471062bf2f5a89340644a809a8470645f6a7359bed7873aa1cd"},"summary":"No heuristic freshness and no stale-if-error: an answer with only Last-Modified is revalidated on every use, and an upstream failure is not covered by a stale entry","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net_cache.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:47:41.910304Z","id":"b990cd07be731b1d9aa1832308a44c67888f605e51cb75e0bfeea2861545a82f","body":{"detail":"Failure: app A (granted host H) fetches url \"https://H/p\\naccept: image/png\" with no headers; app B, also granted H, fetches \"https://H/p\" with header accept: image/png. key_of hashes req.url as given (web/shell/src/caps/net.ts fetchFor sends req.url unchanged; crates/clax-server/src/routes/net.rs fetch builds FetchRequest from b.url) followed by \"\\n<name>: <value>\", so both requests hash the same bytes. The url crate (2.5.8, as locked) strips ASCII tab and newline while parsing: Url::parse(\"https://tile.example.com/1/2/3.png\\naccept: image/png\") gives https://tile.example.com/1/2/3.pngaccept:%20image/png. A's fetch goes to that path, its 200 passes same_url (res.url equals the parsed URL) and is stored under B's key, and B is answered with A's chosen resource until it expires. B's host check passes, so the module's guarantee (a hit only after the asking app's own check) does not prevent it. Fix: hash the parsed https_url(...).as_str() rather than req.url, and length-prefix (or JSON-encode) each field so no field can spell a separator; a test with a newline in the URL would pin it.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":68},"content_hash":"056a478c637b3f463eaeadfade8ec6036dfc2933288888e36ac4cf4e3f3436a5"},"summary":"The cache key hashes the raw URL string and the headers joined by newlines, so one app can poison another app's entry with a different path on the same host","tags":["review","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net_cache.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:47:41.910483Z","id":"7afe40898324ffd0024a77c70afc178ef4c803e5356d29930b24e8bb6b08f42c","body":{"detail":"ac3d4f94 describes the leak as timing and as 'that a public URL was fetched'. Two things make it stronger. (1) A fresh hit is answered by Entry::response (net_cache.rs:188) with no request upstream and an age header computed from the daemon's own received time, so a page can read hit or miss from one call, without timing. (2) Tile URLs encode the place: an app granted tile.openstreetmap.org can ask for tiles around a guessed area and learn which ones another app (for example a location app centred on the user's position) has shown within their lifetime. Probing misses fetches real tiles, so it is noisy and bounded by the guess, but it is a cross-app location channel. Options: key per artifact (ac3d4f94), drop the age header on hits and accept the timing channel, or keep it shared and record a waiver.","kind":"concern","references":"ac3d4f94e3617135af904664f9edc2383c2254fdbf397266aea24292c89b45fd","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":68},"content_hash":"056a478c637b3f463eaeadfade8ec6036dfc2933288888e36ac4cf4e3f3436a5"},"summary":"The shared cache's cross-app leak is a direct hit/miss oracle, and for map tiles it reveals where another app's user looked","tags":["review","security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:47:41.910546Z","id":"297aa05e97e7b580c632c960f5eb53150c9e3ea42552feea35dab7a4bc6a97db","body":{"detail":"cached() adds Entry::validators() (If-None-Match, If-Modified-Since) to req.headers; run() drops them on a redirect to another origin (CROSS_ORIGIN_KEPT, net.rs:328) but keeps them on a same-origin one. When the cached URL now redirects to another path on its host, that path receives the ETag and date of a different resource; if it answers 304, same_url is false, storable(304) is false, the entry is removed and the bodiless 304 is returned to a page that never sent a conditional request. Strip the added validators on any hop after the first, or on a 304 with a different final URL refetch without them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":505},"end":{"line":528},"content_hash":"eda64d8472fad1fc2b23677e6e4d737594f07db72df672441ab4e533f7f9c2cd"},"summary":"A stale entry's validators follow a same-origin redirect, and a 304 from the redirect target reaches a page that sent no validators","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net_cache.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:47:41.910587Z","id":"9c216eab45c441fbb29537e69ac032c0211d00df25be6fc1b78262c1bbf6471b","body":{"detail":"put() writes a .tmp file and renames it without sync_all, and Entry records no body length. After a power loss a renamed file can be shorter than written; get() parses the JSON line and serves whatever follows as the body (a partial tile or JSON). Recording the body length in Entry and dropping a file whose remainder differs (or syncing before the rename) closes it.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":326},"end":{"line":364},"content_hash":"1a3146ab802bcc0f28156bfc54e59efe2591cf2507f4d981eeea48c3ed77d020"},"summary":"An entry file cut short by a crash is served as a truncated body","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net_cache.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:28:14.730861Z","id":"2f48d6c0e9aa61d813b5fc0a0ff265e9675e0a7d8f568ad9b22eea11de31d821","body":{"detail":"Implemented in 20e1ed98c3fc: key_of(app, req) hashes the artifact ID; crates/clax-server/src/routes/net.rs fetch passes the ID in the request path. A draft uses its own ID, not its live app's: it needs no lookup, and a draft written by the agent cannot learn what the live app fetched; the cost is that a draft refetches tiles its app already has, bounded by the same LRU. Update-check drafts with inherit_net false never reach the cache (not_granted before any fetch).","kind":"comment","references":"7afe40898324ffd0024a77c70afc178ef4c803e5356d29930b24e8bb6b08f42c","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-15): per-app cache. Every entry is keyed by the asking artifact's ID as well, so one app cannot observe another's hits; the 100 MiB global cap and LRU stay.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net_cache.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:28:14.730950Z","id":"e17449c88b28ed02aceefc95aca7a28c673db6a5dc369eee33cd2b764153fad2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc per the owner's per-app decision: net_cache::tests::one_app_never_gets_another_apps_entry passes (app B misses after app A's fill; A still hits). cargo test -p clax-server --lib net: 20 passed.","supersedes":"7afe40898324ffd0024a77c70afc178ef4c803e5356d29930b24e8bb6b08f42c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net_cache.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:28:14.732512Z","id":"002df2f77b920f3897d10b8d7dc0c62c315988f095972cc144d9319a3c4dd846","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"The alternative was taken (owner decision 2026-10-15): entries are per artifact since 20e1ed98c3fc; one_app_never_gets_another_apps_entry passes.","supersedes":"ac3d4f94e3617135af904664f9edc2383c2254fdbf397266aea24292c89b45fd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net_cache.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:28:14.733950Z","id":"de489e36f58f8a6530b859d2e7721cd7b07a63a03841c935d45ce6d2502b139c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: key_of hashes the app ID, https_url(...).as_str() and each header as length-prefixed fields. net_cache::tests::no_url_or_header_can_spell_another_requests_key passes (the record's newline URL and the plain accept request get different keys, and the planted answer is not served). cargo test -p clax-server --lib net: 20 passed.","supersedes":"b990cd07be731b1d9aa1832308a44c67888f605e51cb75e0bfeea2861545a82f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:28:14.735345Z","id":"8e491e4baff40dddc420697331fed7cd93173cfac33dcc8c2e3cb0bc0fd98234","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: run() drops the cache's validators after the first hop, and a 304 the entry cannot answer is fetched again without them. net_cache::tests::validators_never_follow_a_redirect_and_a_page_never_gets_a_bare_304 passes. cargo test -p clax-server --lib net: 20 passed.","supersedes":"297aa05e97e7b580c632c960f5eb53150c9e3ea42552feea35dab7a4bc6a97db","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/net_cache.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:28:14.736772Z","id":"d62cabe53874dd89cbfcbca7d2995e3ade74f77354511b78dddde1c89bf8a033","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: Entry records body_len, get() drops a file whose body differs, and put() syncs the temp file before the rename. net_cache::tests::an_entry_cut_short_is_dropped_and_fetched_again passes. cargo test -p clax-server --lib net: 20 passed.","supersedes":"9c216eab45c441fbb29537e69ac032c0211d00df25be6fc1b78262c1bbf6471b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:09:51.123481Z","id":"de9a053293b187773855f50754a92702d89332c7c2114d4bf8078ca360e267d6","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1232},"end":{"line":1257},"content_hash":"f1417fb5728fe626e2f3661ee877c6375ec81fdcca0737af7b50b1c42b623136"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"d7f95bedadf8ee7067521b6769eeec03c5406880db5cb6e67cc659a8fcb96c57","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.461273Z","id":"e3054657c3470f7c032ae8a2a54b917f4520b06a503b49b7040559ef27ef5011","body":{"detail":"Before 20e1ed98c3fc the store opened, then daemon.json was written, then the state, journal and tasks started. Now Core::start (serve.rs:342) starts all of them first; if write_daemon_info (:374) or stop_asked (:375) fails, `?` returns with the Core dropped but not stopped: its reaper, sweepers, journal appender and listeners keep running on the caller's runtime, holding the store. For `clax serve` the process exits; for clax-ios (StopOn::Embedded), whose runtime outlives a failed start, a retried clax_start opens a second Store on the same database beside the first's tasks.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":342},"end":{"line":375},"content_hash":"9c97ad14fd0f3b134ea05829c8efff5bcc7ee55a0e270a6e64c498152a757440"},"suggested_fix":"On either error, `core.stop().await` before returning (a small guard, or write daemon.json's error path explicitly).","summary":"serve now starts the core's tasks, journal and listeners before daemon.json, and returns on a write_daemon_info or stop_asked error without stopping them","tags":["review","daemon","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:25:40.453254Z","id":"26418596951a69110d66f3658bf02baae2b16fd79c6b976a225f140f5bf0d670","body":{"detail":"crate::start_listeners (crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs:161-165: AppState::start_listeners in crates/clax-http/src/state.rs:460-475, routes::people::listen, linked::listen) spawns tasks that loop on broadcast receivers and Notify (e.g. crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs:100-125) and watch no shutdown signal. Core::stop aborts only its background tasks and the journal waiter. Measured with tokio's RuntimeMetrics::num_alive_tasks on a current-thread runtime: a Core::start then Core::stop leaves 6 tasks alive (the baseline in crates/clax-server/tests/daemon.rs a_serve_that_fails_after_its_core_started_stops_the_core). The embedded core shuts its own runtime down after close, which drops them; `clax serve` exits. A host whose runtime outlives a stopped core (clax-ios's StopOn::Embedded, or a reopen in one process) keeps them, each holding an AppState clone and its Store Arc, and they still react to the old store's events.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":199},"end":{"line":216},"content_hash":"b1cff0cecad629c400fe818d8f4be039f005d2fab83b1b7cb0f65885831f1123"},"suggested_fix":"Give each listener the core's shutdown receiver (AppState.shutdown) and end its loop on it, or return their JoinHandles from start_listeners for Core::stop to abort; then assert zero alive tasks after stop in crates/clax-server/tests/core_start.rs.","summary":"Core::stop leaves the listeners' tasks running: start_listeners spawns loops that never end, holding AppState and so the store","tags":["review","daemon","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.371873Z","id":"8e5b7038a68f808a0939dbf21fcfd46928f19b0f13b78627654bd77e473fd316","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: everything after Core::start runs in serve_core, and serve stops the core on whatever it returns. crates/clax-server/tests/daemon.rs a_serve_that_fails_after_its_core_started_stops_the_core (daemon.json a non-empty directory) passes; before the fix it saw 17 tasks alive where a stopped core leaves 12.","supersedes":"e3054657c3470f7c032ae8a2a54b917f4520b06a503b49b7040559ef27ef5011","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:42:20.871958Z","id":"1b1b48600a306df769902001b520ce036ce53131c2f7771e08e816aee325d873","body":{"detail":"20e1ed98c3fc moved `core.stop().await` out of serve_core into serve (serve.rs:378-379), after serve_core returns; serve_core's last step removes daemon.json (serve.rs:491-493). Before 20e1ed98c3fc the order was core.stop() (journal segment closed within JOURNAL_STOP_TIMEOUT, 1.5 s, then Store::shutdown) and only then remove_daemon_info. Now daemon.json is gone while the old process still has its journal appender closing its segment and its store open. A client that starts a daemon when it finds no daemon.json (the hooks' and CLI's autostart) can start one in that window: its Store opens the same database (Store takes no exclusive lock, see crates/clax-server/tests/.qual 6c7ee5f4) and its journal appender recovers the journal directory the old one is still writing. `clax stop` is unaffected (crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs waits for the PID). No test pins the order.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":376},"end":{"line":380},"content_hash":"863217de7942c3d1ca85df56d818db31dd004359204da21adfebb13399eb3816"},"suggested_fix":"Have serve_core return whether daemon.json is still this process's, or remove it in serve after core.stop(); add a check to crates/clax-server/tests/daemon.rs that daemon.json is still present while Core::stop runs (for example, the store refuses calls before daemon.json is removed).","summary":"serve now removes daemon.json before Core::stop, so a client may start a second daemon on the home while the first's journal and store are still stopping","tags":["review","daemon","regression","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:42:20.873077Z","id":"67366b3ed8f2100083a2d0cb7e36e236480cc73b899a83b86e5019c2806a8336","body":{"detail":"Embed::close (crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs:354-385) runs Core::stop, then Shared::release (OPEN and core.lock freed), then posts Closed. The listeners are on the Embed's runtime, which ends only when the last Embed clone drops (Inner::drop, core.rs:182-189, shutdown_timeout on a clax-rt-end thread): after `closed`, and never while a safe-API caller keeps an Embed. A clax_embed_open of the same home is admitted as soon as release() runs, so the new core starts while the old listeners still hold the old AppState (its Store Arc, hub and caches) and react to its events. The old store refuses calls after Store::shutdown (pinned by crates/clax-server/tests/core_start.rs stopping_a_core_closes_its_store_and_ends_its_streams), so they cannot write the database, but linked::listen's supervise loop and the pushes/git_remotes listeners can still run work that does not go through the store, and the header's 'tasks stop … the store closes' is not true of them at `closed`. Fix: clax_server::start_listeners, AppState::start_listeners, routes::people::listen and linked::listen return their JoinHandles; Core keeps them with `tasks`; Core::stop aborts them. Pin it by making daemon.rs a_serve_that_fails_after_its_core_started_stops_the_core assert a stopped core leaves the task count it found (not 6 more), and an embed test that close, then the runtime's alive-task count, is back to the open's baseline. Not a phase 1 blocker; it should land before the app reopens a home in one process (a restore or reset path).","kind":"comment","references":"26418596951a69110d66f3658bf02baae2b16fd79c6b976a225f140f5bf0d670","summary":"It matters for the embedded core: at `closed` the listeners still run, beside a reopen of the same home; Core should own their handles and Core::stop abort them","tags":["review","embed","daemon","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:21:49.167875Z","id":"9ea8e3be06a51ae934489293fa58f87f168e6c17f0cee81d64c9a8fa3ceeb8ba","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: serve removes daemon.json, when still this process's, after core.stop() returns; serve_core no longer removes it. Evidence: serve::tests::daemon_json_goes_only_once_the_core_has_stopped (a test-only hook at the end of Core::stop records whether daemon.json exists) failed with the old order (left [false]) and passes; bazelisk test --keep_going //crates/clax-embed:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-store:all //scripts:no_unsafe //scripts:no_unsafe_test //scripts:crate_layers at 0a8d4312d97d: 19 tests pass.","supersedes":"1b1b48600a306df769902001b520ce036ce53131c2f7771e08e816aee325d873","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:21:49.544714Z","id":"b86888b31903f383d5eacbf7de273652a76d420126461dd88a271cee6dce72e4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc and pinned for the embedded core in 0a8d4312d97d: the listener functions return their JoinHandles, Core keeps them with its background tasks, and Core::stop aborts them (and linked::stop the per-remote tasks) and awaits them, up to 250 ms. Evidence: daemon.rs a_serve_that_fails_after_its_core_started_stops_the_core now asserts a stopped core leaves the task count it found (left 6, right 0 before the fix; passes after); core::tests::a_closed_core_leaves_no_task_beside_a_reopen_of_its_home ('6 tasks of the closed core still run' with the old Core::stop; passes after); bazelisk test --keep_going //crates/clax-embed:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-store:all //scripts:no_unsafe //scripts:no_unsafe_test //scripts:crate_layers at 0a8d4312d97d: 19 tests pass.","supersedes":"26418596951a69110d66f3658bf02baae2b16fd79c6b976a225f140f5bf0d670","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:47:40.258314Z","id":"afc3bb9c6864cef962bc17940f17e4ea52112071771f4877e945f6ff4add0a54","body":{"detail":"stop aborts self.tasks, then crate::linked::stop takes Linked::tasks and aborts each handle, then joins only self.tasks. The per-remote tasks are dropped unawaited, so one running on the other worker can still be inside a poll when stop returns. And abort of the supervisor takes effect only at its next yield: supervise (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs, after its awaited store read) locks Linked::tasks and spawns run(...) for each wanted remote synchronously, so if it is mid-poll when stop runs, it can insert a new task after linked::stop emptied the map; nothing aborts that one, and it keeps the old AppState beside a reopen of the home. The doc comment says no task of the core runs after stop returns. daemon.rs a_serve_that_fails_after_its_core_started_stops_the_core and core.rs a_closed_core_leaves_no_task_beside_a_reopen_of_its_home have no linked remote, so neither sees this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":206},"end":{"line":224},"content_hash":"3192967a77d7ec3c9c6185e31f75f659220b81a667a1b5e036854947bea0af97"},"suggested_fix":"Await the supervisor and listener (join with the timeout) before calling linked::stop, then join the per-remote handles linked::stop takes under the same TASKS_STOP_TIMEOUT (have linked::stop return them). A test with one linked artifact and an unreachable remote can assert the alive-task count after stop.","summary":"Core::stop aborts the linked sync's per-remote tasks without awaiting them, and a supervisor mid-poll can spawn one after linked::stop took the map, so a task may outlive stop","tags":["review","daemon","embed","shutdown","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:28:11.678291Z","id":"e5a98b5055bf8e2b0f9dcea08fe777f4122122da680112302cc745c7b2fb68c2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: linked::stop sets Linked::stopped under Linked::tasks' lock and returns the per-remote handles, supervise checks the flag under that lock and starts nothing once it is set, and Core::stop awaits those handles with its own tasks under TASKS_STOP_TIMEOUT. Evidence: crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs a_stopped_sync_ends_its_tasks_and_its_supervisor_starts_none (a linked Pair: stop, then a supervisor pass with the link still connected) failed before at its last assert ('a stopped sync started a task for the remote') and passes after; crates/clax-server/tests/daemon.rs a_stopped_core_leaves_no_task_of_its_linked_sync (a Core with a connected, unreachable remote and a linked artifact: the alive-task count right as stop returns equals the count before start) passes; bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-realtime:all: 8 targets pass.","supersedes":"afc3bb9c6864cef962bc17940f17e4ea52112071771f4877e945f6ff4add0a54","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:26.925981Z","id":"76468926fcef179b08b6b31416cff1aa86979df1b8d87182245b1e02c789ab82","body":{"detail":"serve() registers SIGTERM with tokio::signal::unix::signal (line 462) and awaits it only inside the graceful-shutdown select (lines 467-483). Tokio installs a process-wide handler that replaces the default disposition for the rest of the process (https://docs.rs/tokio/latest/tokio/signal/unix/fn.signal.html, Caveats), so after a /api/admin/shutdown request (or a first signal) has fired that select, further SIGTERMs and Ctrl-Cs are swallowed. After the bounded drain (DRAIN_TIMEOUT 5 s) and journal wait (JOURNAL_STOP_TIMEOUT 1.5 s), drain_store.shutdown() (line 507) waits for queued store jobs with no bound. A replacing client (crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs:365-420, stop_for_replacement) posts the shutdown, waits 7 s, then sends SIGTERM and waits 3 s: when a store job (an optimize, a large publish, a backfill step) keeps the drain past 7 s, that SIGTERM does nothing, the replacement fails, and its error tells the user to run `kill <pid>`, which sends the same ignored SIGTERM. The JOURNAL_STOP_TIMEOUT doc (lines 28-35) promises the whole shutdown stays within 6.5 s, which the unbounded store drain does not keep.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":462},"end":{"line":512},"content_hash":"51f72da8ca58d652963c339ae6e756779f1eca455b231f59f5b18757034b8872"},"suggested_fix":"Keep listening for SIGTERM/SIGINT after shutdown begins and exit the process (std::process::exit) on a second signal, and bound the store drain with a timeout (spawn_blocking + tokio::time::timeout) so the documented 6.5 s holds; log what was left unfinished.","summary":"Once shutdown has begun, SIGTERM and Ctrl-C no longer stop the daemon, and the store drain after the connection drain has no deadline","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:26.926111Z","id":"6243a11b66ae507c1f3c70d4442e0f7c5920c9a89e47c94d099ffa46f0da749b","body":{"detail":"A push with no link keys its first version `clax-push:<aid>:<n>:new:-` (version_key, lines 800-807; new_target, lines 1180-1184). The remote keeps publish keys per agent token forever (clax_store publish_keys, read by crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:199-223 `replayed`), and replays the version that key made while that artifact exists. Sequence: push (no link) creates public A1 under key ...:1:new:-; the owner unlinks (routes/remotes.rs:422-439, which deletes the remote_links row); a later push has no link again, sends ...:1:new:-, gets A1's version 1 replayed, records the link to A1, and replays its later versions under keys ...:<n>:A1, so the owner's new push lands on the old public copy (with any comments and changes others made there) rather than a fresh one. The same happens after mode `new` moved the link to A2 and A2 was unlinked: the next push re-links A1, not A2. Whether re-linking is wanted after an unlink is not stated anywhere; the version_key doc says a push as new gets a fresh key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1180},"end":{"line":1184},"content_hash":"1b88ab832c6c8f88c2a5045b7aa2365b1d0ab757c1e65a3d39ba32ad0e191f33"},"suggested_fix":"Give each new-public-artifact attempt a key component that changes per link generation (for example a random nonce or the unlink time stored when the link is removed, or a counter of links made for this artifact and remote), or, if re-linking the old copy is intended, say so in the version_key and unlink docs and in the push result.","summary":"A push after unlinking reuses the first push's idempotency key and silently re-links the oldest public artifact instead of making a new one","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:26.926174Z","id":"3896186b2dabd03580c4d91761535dcc7bbc40e4290d656014ba731204113b15","body":{"detail":"routes() applies agent::verify_layer as a route_layer and then hide_live_pages and extension::gateway (lines 541-561, commented 'on every route (spec §6.6)'), but wrap() merges crate::hosted::router (line 686) into the already-layered inner router, so /api/hosted/*, /auth/github, its callback, /setup, /signin*, /join/*, /device, /terms and /privacy see none of them. A Clax-Grant request reaches a hosted handler with an unverified GrantHead (no signature or nonce check), and an agent token reaches it without verify_bearer's per-route `need!` refusal, body gate or use recording; revoke_own_token (hosted.rs:589-609) relies on the BearerGrant extension that agent::authenticate left. Today's hosted handlers either refuse Authorization (browser_only) or use only the bearer lookup, so nothing is exposed now, but the next hosted handler that reads VerifiedGrant, or assumes the extension gateway ran, gets an unverified or missing credential with no sign of it here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":683},"end":{"line":711},"content_hash":"8db129b3c69f0e853f6b415438770e9d07c2ee186e41ec054b61fecaa79a264d"},"suggested_fix":"Merge the hosted router inside routes() before the route_layer and outer layers (or apply the same layers to it in wrap()), and give the hosted routes entries in agent::ROUTES so an agent credential is refused or admitted per route like every other; or correct the comment at lines 541-543 to name the hosted routes as outside it.","summary":"Hosted mode's routes are merged outside the route layers that the router documents as covering every route: agent verification, the extension gateway and the live-page filter","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:26.926266Z","id":"2eee10bb2c9c7bf4bb4b748f27f29329001690cbd1d1f55e7c8beb299f23a298","body":{"detail":"On Stop::Unreachable (lines 283-285) and on a failed feedback poll (lines 330-334) run() sets sync.client = None and clears watched without calling end_session; the next cycle's connect() (lines 529-546) registers a fresh 'clax-sync' session with session_for and watches every linked public artifact again. The dropped session stays live on the remote until its idle reaper ends it, still watching the same artifacts, so a flaky network or a remote answering 5xx/429 (classify, lines 245-252) leaves several clax-sync sessions there at once, and with 429 each retry adds load by registering another session. Only Stop::Gone calls Sync::end (lines 279-281). The agent sessions in sync.agents are kept, so only the sync's own session leaks. Distinct from the unlink case in the open record on linked.rs:1173-1185.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":279},"end":{"line":339},"content_hash":"fbd142f92c8b9afdc741edbda86c10545a4a9eb868ed2ae58bc72fcb77e1f850"},"suggested_fix":"Before dropping the client on an outage, try end_session on it (best effort, bounded), or keep the client and its session across a failed poll and re-register only when the remote refuses the session as unknown.","summary":"Each reconnect of a linked-threads sync drops its remote sessions without ending them, leaving orphan sessions (and their watches) on the public Clax","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:26.926331Z","id":"57d20264296ef283e888b09a44f8be5b9ae44f5533f0e5b6aebb4d4d4b5a1756","body":{"detail":"Client::send reads at most MAX_ANSWER_BYTES and maps a cut-off or unparseable body to Value::Null (lines 333-336), then returns Ok(Null) for any 2xx (lines 337-339); the test at lines 1372-1379 pins this. Callers read fields off it as if absent: linked.rs:1401-1413 takes `v[\"threads\"]` as empty and `next_cursor` as none, so a public artifact whose page of up to 200 threads serializes past 4 MiB (comments are up to 10,000 characters each, clax-store/src/threads.rs:18) is read as having no threads on every cycle, with no error, no status and no cursor movement; its threads never come down. A question copy read as Null is taken as still open (linked.rs:1206).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":317},"end":{"line":339},"content_hash":"cbab4f3c1af3648247fd99fa343e0fc5dcd1362d91023e002e80e38cc911e171"},"suggested_fix":"Return a RemoteFail (code `too_large` or `bad_answer`) for a 2xx body that was cut off or is not JSON, as get_bytes already does for its cap; let the linked read lower its page size on `too_large`.","summary":"A 2xx answer that passes the 4 MiB cap or is not JSON is returned as success with a null body, so the linked-threads read silently mirrors nothing","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:26.926400Z","id":"dde37ee73f204ddfc2c73f50dc382a2c01454ea3e8729e5617baf7d8425200ed","body":{"detail":"The module doc (lines 29-32) and safe_id (lines 1645-1649) say a remote's IDs are used in paths only when they are letters and digits; mirror() (line 1436) and ask_there() (line 1354) check them, and public.rs remote_id (lines 855-865) checks artifact IDs. Sync::send's \"thread\" arm takes v[\"thread\"][\"id\"] as is (line 941) and acks it as the link's remote_thread_id, which the comment, resolve and reopen arms then splice into /api/artifacts/{raid}/threads/{rtid}/... (lines 958-1017). A remote answering an ID with '/', '..', '?' or '#' points those requests (with the agent token) at other routes of the remote than the thread's; the harm stays within that remote, but the rule the module states does not hold.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":941},"end":{"line":951},"content_hash":"0f2f2dd42a9a2ecd9293d5956a8e4c9ffa7e2b1b6b3d25a4287c6654431c7013"},"suggested_fix":"Filter rtid (and rcid) through safe_id at line 941 and treat a non-conforming answer as Sent::Refused(\"the remote answered no thread\").","summary":"The remote thread ID from an up-sent thread's answer is stored and later put in request paths without the safe_id check the rest of the module applies","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:26.926447Z","id":"8619f42c7b5e5c7bb7caeafbf897642af4a9e182699e515c0fb6036a5f4f92e7","body":{"detail":"test_delay (line 580) and test_sleep (line 622) call tokio::time::sleep, and test_slow_publish calls std::thread::sleep (line 639). These are compiled into any debug build, including the wasm32 Durable Object (no target cfg on them, and test_sleep/test_slow_publish are mounted whenever debug_assertions is on, lines 333-336). crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs:48-62 says server code reaches the runtime only through clax_rt because tokio's timer and std sleeps do not work on wasm32; a token-holding call to /api/_test/sleep/<ms> on a debug Worker panics the isolate instead of sleeping.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":564},"end":{"line":660},"content_hash":"ff7538f19dbf946d48c9fb63c45d0dc6b81bdb94933c74ea8952815040710588"},"suggested_fix":"Use clax_rt::time::sleep in test_delay and test_sleep, and either gate test_slow_publish on not(target_arch = \"wasm32\") or replace its std::thread::sleep with an await before the store call.","summary":"The debug test routes sleep on tokio and std directly, which panics on wasm32 where the crate docs require clax_rt","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:26.926503Z","id":"00b09c6e3a54ea569ba0928720fb39f37e3ad28e41bb6deab702b867a082845c","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-rt/src/lib.rs:72-88 defines sendable with the same contract (SendWrapper on wasm32, identity natively, plus a SendOnNative bound); crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs:64-67 documents clax_rt::sendable as the way server code makes a fetch future Send. public.rs keeps its own copy (lines 53-64), and github.rs:137 and linked.rs (lines 464, 467, 512, 539, 566, 571, 618, 655 and on) reach it as crate::public::sendable, so GitHub sign-in depends on the remote-push module for a runtime helper, and routes/mcp_http.rs:363 uses the other one.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"b2d036e80bb11d7c7ea701dc58a49851949424fdc06b15bed225340391f4f525"},"suggested_fix":"Delete public::sendable and call clax_rt::sendable everywhere.","summary":"public::sendable duplicates clax_rt::sendable, which the crate docs name as the seam, and github.rs and linked.rs import it from public","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:26.926564Z","id":"cde31feb0ced32356c130065617bbc53d0e47ed19fac5dc39c0319a7ee8ddb72","body":{"detail":"From<ApiError> for Stop maps every ApiError to Stop::Unreachable (lines 238-242), and cycle() propagates store_call failures with `?` (for example lines 634-637, 668, 702-704). run() then backs off as for an outage, records last_error, and once the backoff reaches BACKOFF_CAP marks every waiting row and question copy failed with the message 'Not sent: <name> unreachable' (lines 296-305), naming the remote for a fault that is this daemon's own database.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":238},"end":{"line":242},"content_hash":"5f35988f842a935cb4d36171856e6ca15183a3937b1543a3cb13820808de703b"},"suggested_fix":"Give Stop a Local(String) variant for store errors, keep the backoff for it, but record the store's message as the reason instead of the remote being unreachable.","summary":"A local store error in a sync cycle is treated as the remote being unreachable, and after the backoff cap marks the outbox 'Not sent: <remote> unreachable'","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:26.926641Z","id":"f0c9f65d65e9ffa5c09202c99054a6028f831b0b87b7ebe69ef9300065db8182","body":{"detail":"gate (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs, the `own` expression after the HostedRequest insert) lists /api/hosted/, /setup, /signin, /device, /signin/, /join/, /auth/github, the GitHub callback, /terms and /privacy as hosted mode's own routes, which skip member_gate and guest_need. router() here mounts exactly those today. A route added here outside /api/hosted/ (a new page or auth path) without the matching edit in the other crate is sent through member_gate or guest_need, which refuse or redirect it, and no test names the pairing.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1192},"end":{"line":1247},"content_hash":"59fe7f0550fc1b5795267f1cb572e5c1b3c27ff5266093ae41c2dc77114cc138"},"suggested_fix":"Export the non-/api/hosted/ paths as one const slice from clax_http::hosted, use it in gate's `own` check and in a test here that every route router() mounts is either under /api/hosted/ or in that slice.","summary":"The hosted router's paths are listed again by hand in clax_http::hosted::gate's `own` check, with nothing tying the two lists together","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:04:44.252210Z","id":"d3f420e5ac8f3ac985b847dbce00d3f27d9a5246315e31e10548c54735e5b52a","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs:462 registers SIGTERM via tokio::signal::unix::signal; it and tokio::signal::ctrl_c() are awaited only in the select at lines 467-479, after which nothing listens but tokio's process-wide handler stays installed. Line 507 runs drain_store.shutdown() under spawn_blocking with no timeout; crates/clax-store/src/exec.rs:1024-1031 calls Workers::drain (exec.rs:765-780), which joins every worker thread with no deadline. crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs:395-410 (stop_for_replacement) waits 7 s, sends SIGTERM, waits 3 s, then bails telling the user to `kill <pid>`. The JOURNAL_STOP_TIMEOUT doc (serve.rs:28-35) claims the whole shutdown stays within 6.5 s, which line 507 does not bound.","kind":"comment","references":"76468926fcef179b08b6b31416cff1aa86979df1b8d87182245b1e02c789ab82","summary":"confirmed: after the graceful-shutdown select fires, SIGTERM/Ctrl-C stay caught by tokio's handler and the store drain is unbounded","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:04:44.252630Z","id":"5957e42610e855f65f87390134755045cd45d683e90121866587ea26fcd8203b","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:1133-1137 starts a push with no link at version 1; lines 1181-1184 key it `new:-`, and lines 1214/1219 build version_key(aid, 1, \"new:-\"). Run::send (lines 1033-1040) posts /api/artifacts with that key; on the remote, routes/artifacts.rs:199-223 `replayed` returns the version publish_keys recorded for that grant and key while the artifact exists. publish_keys rows are never deleted (only SELECT at clax-store/src/remotes.rs:588 and INSERT OR IGNORE at :602 touch the table). Store::unlink_remote (clax-store/src/linked.rs:467-482) deletes only the remote_links row and does not change the agent token, so the grant and key repeat. Later versions then go through Run::send's Some(t) arm with version_key(aid, n, A1) (public.rs:1044), also replayed.","kind":"comment","references":"6243a11b66ae507c1f3c70d4442e0f7c5920c9a89e47c94d099ffa46f0da749b","summary":"confirmed: an unlinked artifact's next push sends the same new:- key and gets the old public artifact's version replayed","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:04:44.252827Z","id":"b7218fe66d44d7752ad577a083ea4db7ce3832e2871074517cfd0214ae2162f1","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs:541-561 applies agent::verify_layer as a route_layer and hide_live_pages and extension::gateway as layers inside routes(); axum's layer/route_layer wrap only routes present when called. wrap() (router.rs:683-689) then does inner.merge(crate::hosted::router(...)), so the routes of crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1193-1247 get only wrap()'s settle_layer, agent::authenticate and hosted::gate. revoke_own_token (hosted.rs:589-609) reads the BearerGrant extension that agent::authenticate sets; no hosted handler reads VerifiedGrant today (grep of hosted.rs finds only BearerGrant), so nothing is exposed now, matching the concern's severity.","kind":"comment","references":"3896186b2dabd03580c4d91761535dcc7bbc40e4290d656014ba731204113b15","summary":"confirmed: hosted routes are merged after routes() applied verify_layer, hide_live_pages and the extension gateway","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:04:44.253065Z","id":"280b7479ce4148835a751b666d24fa30987b6d8cc871831ea6d473bdb03b5503","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs:283-285 (Stop::Unreachable) and 330-334 (poll error) set sync.client = None and clear watched; only Stop::Gone (279-281) calls Sync::end (462-473), which calls end_session. connect() (529-546) then makes a new Client and calls session_for(SYNC_HARNESS, SYNC_NAME). Neither public.rs nor linked.rs has an `impl Drop` that ends the session (grep finds none), so each outage leaves the old session to the remote's idle reaper. classify (245-252) treats 5xx and 429 as Unreachable.","kind":"comment","references":"2eee10bb2c9c7bf4bb4b748f27f29329001690cbd1d1f55e7c8beb299f23a298","summary":"confirmed: Unreachable and a failed poll drop the sync client without ending its remote session","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:04:44.253245Z","id":"5c9fab941d068cf2502f0c973e1a5e1fd0e5310a38bb9b759d25e9cdffeb77df","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:333-339: read_capped (228-243) returns Ok(None) past MAX_ANSWER_BYTES (212, 4 MiB), and a body that does not parse becomes Value::Null; any 2xx then returns Ok(v). The test at public.rs:1372-1378 asserts get() of a body past the cap is Ok(Null). linked.rs:1401-1413 reads v[\"threads\"] as empty and v[\"next_cursor\"] as absent, so the cycle ends with no error. One narrowing: an answer whose Content-Length exceeds the cap is refused earlier (public.rs:322-331) as an `unreachable` RemoteFail, so the silent case is a chunked or compressed answer, or a 2xx that is not JSON (an HTML page from a proxy), not every oversized page.","kind":"comment","references":"57d20264296ef283e888b09a44f8be5b9ae44f5533f0e5b6aebb4d4d4b5a1756","summary":"confirmed: a 2xx body past the cap without Content-Length, or not JSON, is returned as Ok(Null)","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:04:44.253415Z","id":"f6a223e056dd3be0205db8b0b924707f26f21baca0e2cf3916454ca4ea39b809","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs:941-947 takes v[\"thread\"][\"id\"] and comments[0].id as answered and passes them to ack_outbox. The comment arm builds /api/artifacts/{raid}/threads/{rtid}/comments (line 970) and the other arms /api/artifacts/{raid}/threads/{rtid}/{kind} (line 1017) from lt.remote_thread_id. safe_id (1645-1649) is applied only at lines 1354 and 1436.","kind":"comment","references":"dde37ee73f204ddfc2c73f50dc382a2c01454ea3e8729e5617baf7d8425200ed","summary":"confirmed: the up-sent thread's remote ID is stored and spliced into paths without safe_id","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:04:44.253573Z","id":"922f5c481aad70f81bcb1f00faf0508208a9043fccbaed14fb5f8cd94ee642d5","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs:580 (test_delay) and the test_sleep body call tokio::time::sleep; test_slow_publish calls std::thread::sleep; they are cfg(debug_assertions) only, with no target cfg, and mounted at router.rs:333-336. `cargo tree --offline --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -e normal,features -i tokio` in crates/clax-worker shows tokio feature \"time\" enabled (via rmcp and tokio-stream), so a debug wasm32 build compiles these, and on the Worker there is no tokio runtime for the timer (tokio::time::sleep panics outside a runtime). crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs:48-62 requires clax_rt::time for timers.","kind":"comment","references":"8619f42c7b5e5c7bb7caeafbf897642af4a9e182699e515c0fb6036a5f4f92e7","summary":"confirmed: debug test routes call tokio::time::sleep and std::thread::sleep, which compile for wasm32 but have no runtime there","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:04:44.253747Z","id":"e46c6130710479d29c035df53cc51666f502b7a40cabc5ef52ac284b6d5566fe","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:53-64 defines sendable (identity natively, SendWrapper on wasm32); crates/clax-rt/src/lib.rs:72-88 defines the same, with a SendOnNative bound. crates/clax-server/src/github.rs:137 and 23 lines of linked.rs and 4 of routes/remotes.rs use crate::public::sendable, while routes/mcp_http.rs:363 uses clax_rt::sendable. crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs:64-67 names clax_rt::sendable as the seam.","kind":"comment","references":"00b09c6e3a54ea569ba0928720fb39f37e3ad28e41bb6deab702b867a082845c","summary":"confirmed: public::sendable duplicates clax_rt::sendable and other modules import it from public","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:04:44.253909Z","id":"a43dd75447a8311860a994cc00f5c04b50b4385bcb7bfebe1f1d8978ace849b9","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs:238-242 maps every ApiError to Stop::Unreachable; cycle() propagates store_call errors with `?` (lines 634-637, 668, 702-704). run() (283-305) records the message as last_error, backs off, and at BACKOFF_CAP calls outbox_failed_all and linked_questions_failed_all with format!(\"Not sent: {name} unreachable\").","kind":"comment","references":"cde31feb0ced32356c130065617bbc53d0e47ed19fac5dc39c0319a7ee8ddb72","summary":"confirmed: store errors become Stop::Unreachable and, at the backoff cap, mark rows 'Not sent: <remote> unreachable'","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:04:44.254083Z","id":"12bbea84ffa2a41dd54b5f40a2fb9575ba56cb04b78439dc3a7fa082bfd7a2e8","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1554-1562 lists /api/hosted/, /setup, /signin, /device, /signin/, /join/, /auth/github, github::CALLBACK_PATH, /terms and /privacy; crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1193-1247 mounts exactly those plus /api/hosted/* routes. Nothing shares a constant between them; a non-own path with a member goes to member_gate (clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1563-1564).","kind":"comment","references":"f0c9f65d65e9ffa5c09202c99054a6028f831b0b87b7ebe69ef9300065db8182","summary":"confirmed: gate's `own` list repeats the hosted router's paths by hand","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:36:49.492701Z","id":"243103bb77911deec1f763f90804b6082ee108baeaa06a520dca042c8cc0ca9d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:67a44a573","summary":"Fixed: hosted routes merge in routes() before agent::verify_layer, hide_live_pages and extension::gateway; agent credentials get 403 on hosted routes except the self-revoke. api_hosted::an_agent_token_on_the_api_reaches_only_a_grants_routes passes.","supersedes":"3896186b2dabd03580c4d91761535dcc7bbc40e4290d656014ba731204113b15","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:36:49.536656Z","id":"f813d53b41d14d28e475f3f333e6940c4365280accb3d54c31d8d9fdedf26919","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4caee173b","summary":"Fixed: debug test routes sleep on clax_rt::time and slow_publish is native-only; router::tests::the_routes_sleep_on_clax_rt passes.","supersedes":"8619f42c7b5e5c7bb7caeafbf897642af4a9e182699e515c0fb6036a5f4f92e7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:36:49.660103Z","id":"c28f01074a5297dc8fe76f0e3494b55fa29e071d4151ba1621f544a54b89c5f4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:67a44a573","summary":"Fixed: clax_http::hosted::own_route and its path lists replace the gate's hand-written check; hosted::tests::the_gate_takes_every_hosted_route_as_its_own and hosted_modes_own_routes pass.","supersedes":"f0c9f65d65e9ffa5c09202c99054a6028f831b0b87b7ebe69ef9300065db8182","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:36:50.199102Z","id":"95e35c30909ce369af0c02eace6b00a231a63ec057e8007ee5baad337bb15ab1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:142aef501","summary":"Fixed (8996c4d29, 142aef501, 5d9410156): a signal after shutdown began exits, the store stop is bounded, and clax serve shuts its runtime down in the background; serve::tests signal tests and cli shutdown::shutdown_leaves_a_store_call_that_does_not_finish_to_the_exit pass (fails with drop(rt)).","supersedes":"76468926fcef179b08b6b31416cff1aa86979df1b8d87182245b1e02c789ab82","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:12:47.681683Z","id":"54b05a4be4e1d3e9b7a014ab3cbd487af009db16255026fbfd5042141fc263e0","body":{"detail":"No existing table survives an unlink with a per-(artifact, remote) value: Store::unlink_remote (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs) deletes the remote_links row. The fix tried: a table remote_unlinks(artifact_id, remote_id, n) bumped in unlink_remote and deleted in remove_remote, read by push() into new_target as `new:-:<n>` when n > 0 (keeping `new:-` for n = 0, so keys made before stay valid), and the version_key doc updated. A test in crates/clax-server/tests/api_remotes.rs pushes, unlinks, pushes and asserts a different remote_artifact_id; against the current code it fails with left == right (the first public artifact taken back). Held back so as not to add a migration number while another branch's migrations are installed on devices.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1197},"end":{"line":1201},"content_hash":"1b88ab832c6c8f88c2a5045b7aa2365b1d0ab757c1e65a3d39ba32ad0e191f33"},"summary":"Fixing record 6243a11b (a push after an unlink re-links the first public artifact) needs a per-link-generation key component, which needs schema","tags":["linked-threads","revisit:after-flutter-app-migrations","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:12:47.681922Z","id":"a90e52aa27316a038a5218595e84f3f5d0724fa25ce2db35a17b6334f8da1318","body":{"detail":"Sync::question (and ask_there, reask, question_done, agent_client) return Result<_, String> and map store errors with `.map_err(|e| e.message)`; questions() turns any Err into Stop::Unreachable and records it with linked_question_attempted. Outbox sends and direct store calls now stop as Stop::Local (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs, Stop), naming the store's error; the question path does not, so a local database fault there still shows the remote unreachable and, at the backoff cap, marks copies 'Not sent: <remote> unreachable'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1184},"end":{"line":1189},"content_hash":"b4e2207358358c8c2baef50d3017cf113d8e14a195009eda7668b5c576d58fc8"},"suggested_fix":"Return Result<_, Stop> from question() and its helpers as send() does, letting `?` turn store errors into Stop::Local, and record linked_question_attempted only for Stop::Unreachable.","summary":"A store error while handling a linked question copy is still reported as the remote unreachable","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:02:15.244554Z","id":"bd101e467c9dd3a1bac05068b8036ebbabb68b4a0f8fb3332d10946e7feb50e7","body":{"detail":"connect() maps any session_for failure to Stop::Unreachable (line 626, classify or the remote's message), so a 403 (for example a grant that no longer may register sessions) is retried at BACKOFF_CAP (300 s, line 80) indefinitely and the link shows the remote unreachable rather than refused. A 4xx other than 401/429 is not an outage: it could stop the remote's task with an owner-facing error until the owner acts (Retry or reconnect).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":617},"end":{"line":630},"content_hash":"de297c59688bd9a632f60261aa5eeb196bfabe5f4e3e1a9e61e1a41e4eab3b6b"},"summary":"A permanent refusal registering the sync's session backs off at the 300 s cap forever","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:02:15.244793Z","id":"ff2d094e296c260cbc088cf8e33bca274b14c5a33b042fb283ad247197f1d4ba","body":{"detail":"read() sets Linked::read_errors (crates/clax-realtime/src/linked.rs) when a thread's page of one is past the 4 MiB answer cap, and GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/remotes answers it as links[].read_error (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs:347, typed in web/shell/src/ui/publish-api.ts), but web/shell/src/ui/Publish.svelte does not show it, so the owner sees a healthy link whose new threads stop coming down. The entry is also kept when the link ends or its artifact 404s (line 1486 returns before clearing it); it is in memory only and gone at restart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1464},"end":{"line":1525},"content_hash":"b9966ff828950c9675152789a8c6414212ab4644fe2e4bc67a6068be9c8dbab0"},"summary":"A link's read_error is shown nowhere in the web shell, and outlives its link","tags":["linked-threads","ui","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:23:05.637413Z","id":"3a1c7d176a5b0aab28d5093def357be991e8e912ab44a3c12998d7c2590317f5","body":{"detail":"When read() runs out of MAX_PAGES (50) with a next page pending it stores a Resume and the run loop starts the next cycle at once. tests/api_linked.rs threads_after_a_run_of_large_ones_all_come_down covers the page-size reset and the cursor staying until the end, but its read takes about ten pages; reaching the resume path takes more than 50 pages (for example many threads of over 1 MiB in a row), which no test builds. A Resume is in memory only and is not dropped when its link ends.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1567},"end":{"line":1578},"content_hash":"bb625b63f385bb9392fad77ff7e81ba854992992022e93c685278a849a3b4668"},"summary":"A read resumed across cycles is not covered by a test","tags":["linked-threads","tests","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:03:41.517056Z","id":"717c90ad720165b50580c40e818ed276fc06dbba3381edbe72b0eac29406d32e","body":{"detail":"A read that runs out of pages goes on in later cycles (Resume) and, at its end, moves the link's sync cursor to the newest activity it saw. A comment made, between those cycles, on a thread the read had already passed has an activity older than that cursor when a thread read later is newer, so the next read's since filters it out until the thread changes again (or a full read at the backstop, whose since is None). Setting the cursor to the newest activity of the read's first cycle instead would not skip it, but would have the next read go over most of a long read again, and long reads could follow each other; the same race exists, narrower, between the pages of one cycle.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1610},"end":{"line":1629},"content_hash":"2da15565604c6ff00ce5e79a21956356f04ebc81b902665078151c228266a6be"},"summary":"A read spread over several cycles can skip a comment made on a thread it read early","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:03:41.517380Z","id":"eff5fd33091b005e8e38a9299fa467ed416c83a6ffa2442cc74d7db1dcaa7067","body":{"detail":"Linked::set_read_limits (pages of two threads, one page a cycle) makes a read of six threads go on across cycles; Linked::hold_resumed holds one between cycles while its page cursor's thread is deleted there. A Resume is now keyed by link and dropped when its link is gone from links_of_remote. Proposed for closing by the owner.","kind":"comment","references":"3a1c7d176a5b0aab28d5093def357be991e8e912ab44a3c12998d7c2590317f5","summary":"Covered since git:ddb01a270: tests/api_linked.rs a_read_past_its_pages_goes_on_in_the_next_cycles and a_read_whose_page_cursor_is_deleted_there_starts_over","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:38:03.114346Z","id":"152dc4a808aba9c767d0160ebfbcbd94b4aee79ecaeadc40c4c2e8052b9f95c6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:539d77060","summary":"Fixed (539d77060, 6a5af5fbc): the sync keeps its remote session across an outage and replaces only one that is gone; linked::tests::a_heartbeat_keeps_the_session_through_an_outage_and_replaces_one_gone passes. A permanent 403 at registration is concern bd101e46.","supersedes":"2eee10bb2c9c7bf4bb4b748f27f29329001690cbd1d1f55e7c8beb299f23a298","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:38:03.138664Z","id":"78f131b02ca609b25782c49fce2e7ad31390c5c5748ebe204ed2e53870ec47d1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f54d07457","summary":"Fixed: an up-sent thread's remote ID is checked with safe_id before it is stored or put in a path; //crates/clax-server/... pass.","supersedes":"dde37ee73f204ddfc2c73f50dc382a2c01454ea3e8729e5617baf7d8425200ed","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:38:03.163063Z","id":"406c3fd67141b34fcf87c2e5f8bee59a407a62cfdd10484a0314a8e31a300b2a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:93d768879","summary":"Fixed: remote futures use clax_rt::sendable and public::sendable is gone; //crates/clax-server/... pass.","supersedes":"00b09c6e3a54ea569ba0928720fb39f37e3ad28e41bb6deab702b867a082845c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:38:03.187432Z","id":"8d16741237de00b445649c5cf535006818920420fec7dfce451925acb356d684","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ea8bacc06","summary":"Fixed (ea8bacc06, 0ca8369b1, b832806b6, afc366a79): a success answer cut off at the cap or not JSON is refused; an over-cap thread stops only its link's read; the cursor moves only when a read reaches its last page; a refused page cursor restarts the read. api_linked a_thread_past_the_answer_cap_stops_its_links_read_not_the_remotes, threads_after_a_run_of_large_ones_all_come_down, a_read_past_its_pages_goes_on_in_the_next_cycles, a_read_whose_page_cursor_is_deleted_there_starts_over pass.","supersedes":"57d20264296ef283e888b09a44f8be5b9ae44f5533f0e5b6aebb4d4d4b5a1756","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:38:03.211982Z","id":"fef9726bec42de26188e5737143d6bde2ad55fd6d1dc1b00273d1e441c96b20c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"cde31feb0ced32356c130065617bbc53d0e47ed19fac5dc39c0319a7ee8ddb72","summary":"Partly fixed on main in 74203cc4a: a store error in a sync cycle stops it as local, not as the remote unreachable. The rest is concern a90e52aa.","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:38:03.212166Z","id":"149fde67a9291f6d81a9905df3a6c6aed9249f08adec48c3c2d2e604e4bbe5f4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:afc366a79","summary":"Fixed in afc366a79: Resume is keyed by link and dropped when its link is gone, and api_linked::a_read_past_its_pages_goes_on_in_the_next_cycles and a_read_whose_page_cursor_is_deleted_there_starts_over reach the resumed read and pass (see reply eff5fd33).","supersedes":"3a1c7d176a5b0aab28d5093def357be991e8e912ab44a3c12998d7c2590317f5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:26:43.828971Z","id":"8546515fa879699fcc6228af08dd82add193e976794d91ca3aae2e614ab6c0d7","body":{"detail":"A shell reached at a LAN address (or [::1]) has no site origins (artifactOrigin in web/shell/src/origin.ts answers null; boot.rs on_loopback_name), so it frames /c/<id>/v/<n>/ sandboxed on the public host as before site hosts, and without_site_origins lets those requests through; on localhost and 127.0.0.1 /c/ is 404 (crates/clax-server/tests/api_site.rs the_public_host_serves_no_content). The public host therefore still serves any artifact's content by ID to a LAN peer. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md Task 5 removes LAN viewing (403 forbidden_host); remove without_site_origins and the local /c/ routes with it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":717},"end":{"line":740},"content_hash":"e143b6b517563e24e1aecd8b2c3f94a62d3ada7b65d620d3029f10e475b3f4df"},"summary":"A local daemon still serves /c/ content on its public host to a Host other than localhost or 127.0.0.1, for LAN viewers","tags":["site-origins","lan","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:35:28.483626Z","id":"4a4b3b303054fca32546b7ea7237414a8aa14f4fd66fe776b75ab5be11142141","body":{"detail":"without_site_origins (crates/clax-server/src/router.rs:721-744) lets /c/<id>/v/<n>/ and /c/<id>/draft/… through to every Host whose name is not localhost or 127.0.0.1, with no access check: a LAN viewer's address, [::1], and any name a page makes resolve to this machine (DNS rebinding) read any artifact by its ID; on localhost and 127.0.0.1 /c/ is 404 (crates/clax-server/tests/api_site.rs the_public_host_serves_no_content). It is kept for a shell with no site origins (artifactOrigin in web/shell/src/origin.ts answers null off localhost and 127.0.0.1). docs/contract.md (the site bullet of the security rules) says so. Also: in sandbox mode on localhost or 127.0.0.1 the frame loads the artifact's site origin, sandboxed (frame_site in crates/clax-server/src/shell/boot.rs, frameSite in web/shell/src/origin.ts, pinned by web/shell/src/frame-src-cases.json), so where the browser does not resolve <id>.localhost, which is why sandbox mode is chosen, the frame is empty: there is no fallback to /c/ on loopback any more. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md Task 5 removes sandbox mode and LAN viewing (403 forbidden_host); remove without_site_origins and the local /c/ routes with it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":721},"end":{"line":744},"content_hash":"e143b6b517563e24e1aecd8b2c3f94a62d3ada7b65d620d3029f10e475b3f4df"},"summary":"A local daemon still serves /c/ content by ID to any Host but localhost and 127.0.0.1: a LAN peer's, [::1], or a DNS-rebinding name that resolves to this machine","supersedes":"8546515fa879699fcc6228af08dd82add193e976794d91ca3aae2e614ab6c0d7","tags":["site-origins","lan","security","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:39:37.354381Z","id":"776a7c76f8949bfc0f7f37bb03833f9306dd05766183ce7c9a91621ce7796d7b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:86ec4f43","summary":"without_site_origins and every local /c/ route are removed (crates/clax-server/src/router.rs), and a peer of another machine is refused (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs local_peers). Evidence at 86ec4f43: crates/clax-server/tests/api_site.rs the_public_host_serves_no_content (/c/... is 404 under [::1], a LAN Host and a rebinding name) and crates/clax-server/tests/api_content.rs a_lan_viewer_is_refused (403 forbidden_host for /a/<id>, the API and the site host from 192.0.2.7 and 192.168.1.2) pass in bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1..__6; web/e2e/boot.spec.ts 'a page reached under a rebound host name' gets 404 for /c/<id>/v/1/.","supersedes":"4a4b3b303054fca32546b7ea7237414a8aa14f4fd66fe776b75ab5be11142141","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T16:04:20.380835Z","id":"21be03e8d71de14a9551c26657df13767ebf8cdd245561f759a5b4a619e371b0","body":{"detail":"github::start keeps next in the flow cookie and callback redirects to it (crates/clax-server/src/github.rs return_path), but failed() renders a fixed href=\"/auth/github\" and callback does not pass the verified next to it. Likewise a sign-in link or invite made on another device carries no next: a visitor sent to /signin?next=<the /site-signin address> who signs in by a link in another tab returns only when the /signin tab is reloaded (web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte: the status page goes on to next once signed in; web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts exercises that reload).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":369},"end":{"line":369},"content_hash":"2d772c11a7963017c6ecf6c61e911285b7db756ef61991b2f1348bd01601e1cc"},"suggested_fix":"Pass the verified next to failed() and link /auth/github?next=<it> when it is not /.","summary":"The GitHub sign-in failure page's \"Sign in again\" links to /auth/github without the flow's next, so a retry after a failed sign-in lands on the gallery, not the site that sent the browser","tags":["site-origins","hosted","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T16:28:15.055829Z","id":"062c08ca2f1245cc234473bb354d18207ca9c95fd7525f730a64a8be08bb5c7d","body":{"detail":"room::session and RoomSocket recheck a socket's holder on Event::Access only when it was opened on a site host (RoomCheck::site is Some, crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs). A socket opened at the public host's /api/artifacts/<id>/room with a hosted browser session keeps its admission after the share is removed or the browser signs out, until it closes or (on the Worker) the next wake, where room::reopen checks clax_http::hosted::session_reads. The shell no longer opens it (the page's room socket is the bridge's on /_clax/api/room, web/bridge/src/caps/room-socket.ts), so only a same-origin client of the public host reaches it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":522},"end":{"line":522},"content_hash":"795cde207e563b9ce7c3a6fbbd3dbbea70087e9dd51706aefb0dd4c4bada0bbb"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the hosted session's hash in RoomCheck and recheck session_reads on Event::Access, or stop serving the public host's room route to hosted browsers.","summary":"A room socket opened on the public host with a hosted session is not checked again when its person loses access","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:42:52.602181Z","id":"9eae86bcbbb737ae71fba4ff51fae1bc2225eb2a3f1918d3ddb77d746db63a9c","body":{"detail":"poll_sign_in reads the device code, gets the token from POST /api/hosted/device/token, then calls connect_remote, which answers NotFound when the pending row is gone (crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs:274-292, `WHERE id = ?1 AND status = 'pending'`). The token is then dropped without public::revoke. Failure: in the Clax app, Cancel on the connect sheet while a poll is out (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart _cancel → _forget → removeRemote) when the core runs the remove between the poll's token fetch and connect_remote. The account's device list on the remote then shows a 'Clax on <device>' token that no one holds, until it is revoked there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":612},"end":{"line":627},"content_hash":"7958f0c611a844224bf1efcf69007a511262b08eeb5c9993e9a177240e88a8d6"},"suggested_fix":"On connect_remote's NotFound, revoke the fresh token on the remote (public::revoke with a Remote built from r and the token) before answering.","summary":"A sign-in the remote approves after its pending remote was removed leaves an unrevoked agent token on the remote","tags":["area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:26:56.718299Z","id":"bff13b0c042c4c48263683bf92113d480d569f0a010e0140b20d176d32684ecb","body":{"detail":"Apple and Google fetch /.well-known/apple-app-site-association and /.well-known/assetlinks.json with no session, and clax_http::hosted::gate answers 401 sign_in_required to every path guest_need does not know. The routes are mounted outside the gate, the credential checks and agent::authenticate; each handler (crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs apple_app_site_association, assetlinks) checks the Host is the hosted public host itself and takes DeniedToGrants, so grant requests are still refused. The other way is to add both paths to OWN_PAGES (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs) and mount the routes beside the others; that keeps every route behind one gate.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":886},"end":{"line":895},"content_hash":"52705b5ab63856007b2acc846781a4a77646d18d45c422286bfe4f8e38007f93"},"summary":"The app links' /.well-known files are routed ahead of the hosted gate rather than listed in clax_http::hosted::OWN_PAGES","tags":["revisit:crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs OWN_PAGES or guest_need gains public files","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:22:50.565813Z","id":"2c4df0f966f6e4eb5fe69891ae2252c84075f8c00eddda9799a9d125494bfd31","body":{"detail":"POST /api/hosted/device/code takes client_kind from an unauthenticated body. The approval page (web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte, data-testid device-app) tells the approving person that the device may manage the sharing of their apps, so the wider right is shown before it is granted, but nothing proves the sign-in comes from the Clax app. POST /api/remotes on any local daemon passes kind clax-app through (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs add).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1150},"end":{"line":1162},"content_hash":"11c973c839a48e1bfd293e5e08bc2ca11261bb289b3d6e1a99a01a057fca0068"},"summary":"client_kind is the machine's own claim: any Clax (or a script) may name itself clax-app and, once approved, get a token that manages sharing","tags":["security","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:59:16.484455Z","id":"24555b7b58fd58314f02a729e48fc56593fd3e6a9e4aeebe7dd1e8ac644c7b85","body":{"detail":"start_sign_in adds client_kind only when a kind is given, so a daemon's sign-in (no kind) still reaches an older remote. The Clax app always passes kind clax-app (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart addRemote default), and before this change crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs DeviceCodeBody is #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] with no client_kind, so an older remote answers 400 invalid_json and POST /api/remotes surfaces it as a remote refusal. There is no retry without the kind and no wording that says the remote must be upgraded. A remote has to run this change before any app build that connects to it ships.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":557},"end":{"line":561},"content_hash":"fddd313f0a7203b4993cde6cc041907a7a3189be5a126fab618c692a88ef456b"},"suggested_fix":"Ship remotes first; or, on a 400 invalid_json naming client_kind, say the remote is too old to connect the Clax app rather than a generic refusal.","summary":"A clax-app sign-in to a remote older than this change is refused outright: the remote's DeviceCodeBody denies the unknown client_kind field","tags":["compat","remotes","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:06:53.501686Z","id":"824930870465e03f7971311274caa69cbc90ff6b180b7857aea1d152dbcbdba3","body":{"detail":"may_share (with set_link, put_share, delete_share and put_comments through sharer) accepts the owner or the artifact's creator (artifact_created_by) and never asks Rights::allows. A person whose rights the owner narrowed (to read only, or none at their own artifacts) can still share their artifact by a viewer or commenter link, readable by anyone with it. The same holds for a person's own device: a person-device agent token (the Clax app's sign-in, Store::person_device_viewer) reaches these routes as its person (browser_or_device), so it too shares whatever its person made, and for the owner every artifact here, whatever the rights.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":759},"end":{"line":765},"content_hash":"34f4ce85eeb082ad930980e893de68b4eb33428559890a93967c68d937d18799"},"suggested_fix":"For anyone but the owner, also require MemberRights::allows_at with (clax-artifacts, update) at the artifact.","summary":"A person shares their own artifact by link whatever their current rights at it","supersedes":"ebe93fe2768eda2ad0f2666c77b8d11afb6fbe251bd7ea027653cd8c5c4a1c5f","tags":["security","rights","hosted","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:06:53.573498Z","id":"cdeda2aecce0a9e02a37e2b9e32d4ceb470355bd421399160970fd2a845610a0","body":{"detail":"poll_sign_in reads the device code, gets the token from POST /api/hosted/device/token, then calls connect_remote, which answers NotFound when the pending row is gone (crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs:274-292, `WHERE id = ?1 AND status = 'pending'`). The token is then dropped without public::revoke. Failure: in the Clax app, Cancel on the connect sheet while a poll is out (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart _cancel → _forget → removeRemote) when the core runs the remove between the poll's token fetch and connect_remote. The account's device list on the remote then shows a 'Clax on <device>' token that no one holds, until it is revoked there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":622},"end":{"line":637},"content_hash":"7958f0c611a844224bf1efcf69007a511262b08eeb5c9993e9a177240e88a8d6"},"suggested_fix":"On connect_remote's NotFound, revoke the fresh token on the remote (public::revoke with a Remote built from r and the token) before answering.","summary":"A sign-in the remote approves after its pending remote was removed leaves an unrevoked agent token on the remote","supersedes":"9eae86bcbbb737ae71fba4ff51fae1bc2225eb2a3f1918d3ddb77d746db63a9c","tags":["area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:06:53.645086Z","id":"5312916514a6a09eacd7da291fb70b0aa79ef984947443a5b40971df07270737","body":{"detail":"No existing table survives an unlink with a per-(artifact, remote) value: Store::unlink_remote (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs) deletes the remote_links row. The fix tried: a table remote_unlinks(artifact_id, remote_id, n) bumped in unlink_remote and deleted in remove_remote, read by push() into new_target as `new:-:<n>` when n > 0 (keeping `new:-` for n = 0, so keys made before stay valid), and the version_key doc updated. A test in crates/clax-server/tests/api_remotes.rs pushes, unlinks, pushes and asserts a different remote_artifact_id; against the current code it fails with left == right (the first public artifact taken back). Held back so as not to add a migration number while another branch's migrations are installed on devices.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1207},"end":{"line":1211},"content_hash":"1b88ab832c6c8f88c2a5045b7aa2365b1d0ab757c1e65a3d39ba32ad0e191f33"},"summary":"Fixing record 6243a11b (a push after an unlink re-links the first public artifact) needs a per-link-generation key component, which needs schema","supersedes":"54b05a4be4e1d3e9b7a014ab3cbd487af009db16255026fbfd5042141fc263e0","tags":["linked-threads","revisit:after-flutter-app-migrations","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:13:08.379138Z","id":"46b51fdaa67886a6e7104480094747e10777b1f0af6ac98ab5c966f4768260c1","body":{"detail":"Run::send copies meta's description, icon and capabilities into the body only for POST /api/artifacts; POST /api/artifacts/<id>/versions carries title, label, note and files, as clax push always has. Recipients read capabilities from the bundle, so installs are right, but the public page served on the remote keeps the first version's capabilities (a db or net capability added later is missing there).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1242},"end":{"line":1246},"content_hash":"43a69117e091ca10281b41fb31cba47884871b82ab30b74900530f035e57dc7e"},"summary":"An app-mode publish sends description, icon and capabilities only when it creates the public copy: a later version that adds a capability does not reach the live page on the remote","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:13:25.221834Z","id":"0d25705d4faea5009d9a3ec12d964d46cb8414b1e18ea5d5c7fd30d9699bc053","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d1d31c3e8","summary":"The other way was taken: both paths are in clax_http::hosted::OWN_PAGES and mounted beside /a/{aid}/get behind the one gate. get_page.rs well_known tests (including well_known_not_on_a_content_host: 200 on the public host, 404 on [::1]:port and {aid}.localhost:port) pass; with the OWN_PAGES entries removed both well_known tests fail.","supersedes":"bff13b0c042c4c48263683bf92113d480d569f0a010e0140b20d176d32684ecb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:44:35.581045Z","id":"679c8af64c3f8393418081a255a5aab27673037927bcb50dc0d760957e1bc972","body":{"detail":"With no link, version_key names the target new:- (or new:<old raid> for mode new on a link), so after DELETE /api/artifacts/<aid>/remotes/<rid> the next clax push sends the same Idempotency-Key as the first create and the remote answers the old artifact while it still exists. App-mode pushes count earlier copies instead (Store::remote_copies; api_remotes_app::app_push_after_unlink_makes_a_new_copy). The same count would serve here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1457},"end":{"line":1461},"content_hash":"1b88ab832c6c8f88c2a5045b7aa2365b1d0ab757c1e65a3d39ba32ad0e191f33"},"summary":"clax push (modes update and new) after an unlink replays the first public copy instead of making a new one","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:58:52.214390Z","id":"78e6ed551ca8edc1409b237b517cebcc4d56a67203dcd887d67cc8e1c4f86f7d","body":{"detail":"The key names the local version (app_version_key), so after publish v3 on:1 made public version 2 with its answer lost, publish v4 sends a new key with if_version 1 and the remote answers 409, which push_app reports as remote_moved (remote_version 2). Only resending the same version replays. Store::local_twin cannot see it either, since nothing was recorded. The person then sees the Diverged sheet for their own publish.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1605},"end":{"line":1605},"content_hash":"dff86c5eda88cd3ab19e7a80c64778b591f9ee3eb25be95085b39e7608d0ed6d"},"summary":"An app push whose answer was lost, followed by a push of a different local version, answers remote_moved against this device's own public version","tags":["review","app-push","severity:minor","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102030Z","id":"eeb6bffcf13e9425642d99431b8df7abea41c25f297ba9ac942310af3299afd2","body":{"detail":"put_comments (lines 994-995) and list_apps (lines 1029-1031) say an Authorization that is not a person's device's gets 403 browser_required. A non-device agent token never reaches the handler: crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs verify_bearer refuses it 403 forbidden (auth::grants_refused), as crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs plain_agent_token_still_refused_on_sharing asserts and docs/contract.md (Sharing from a device) says. device_code (lines 1139-1140) reads as 400 limit_reached for a client_kind other than clax-app; the handler answers 400 invalid_args, as docs/contract.md says.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":994},"end":{"line":995},"content_hash":"58929e7ef996ac9fb514609555e4981efca9b8d004c11ae9592b94b0c83978b5"},"suggested_fix":"Say 403 forbidden for another agent token in put_comments and list_apps, and split device_code's sentence so client_kind's refusal is invalid_args.","summary":"Doc comments name refusal codes the routes do not give: browser_required for a non-device token, and limit_reached for a bad client_kind","tags":["review","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:49:54.136760Z","id":"2799cec623715dd9d7845c1c09148964434dcb8054bebd82cbb899a50a505b89","body":{"detail":"The mirror takes an agent comment's person from c[\"agent\"][\"person\"]; people's (device) views give it, agent-channel views drop `agent`. A remote linked with a plain token, not a device, therefore keys every agent comment remote:<origin>#*owner: approving that key lets a member's agents through with the owner's. It withholds safely (nothing reads unapproved), but approval is coarser than the hosted Clax's people.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1688},"end":{"line":1692},"content_hash":"10b3cac40b136ae032f4b44ea8c13e283243f46c84c7d2ae2cc6cc0874f6f523"},"summary":"An agent comment read through an agent-channel token carries no `agent`, so its author is keyed as the hosted owner's agent whoever's agent wrote it","tags":["security","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:00:04.846217Z","id":"b8a96b8d4f8fe152916087540e43b00d24055fdc4bc20c98c3ae8399b7d332d3","body":{"detail":"comment_agent (crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs:575-587) returns None when agent_name is NULL. COMMENT_SELECT LEFT JOINs sessions (threads.rs:613-619), and Comment::agent is skip_serializing_if none (crates/clax-core/src/model.rs:231-236), as are replies from before agent names. So the hosted JSON has no `agent` for these, and mirrored_author_key (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:390-405) maps (None, \"agent\") to *owner whatever the hosted session's person was. An approval of remote:<origin>#*owner (named by remote_author_name after the newest comment under that key) then also lets through any member's agent comment that lost its session's name. The hosted Clax could serve the agent's person apart from its name (a top-level agent_person on agent comments in people's views), and the sync would read that instead.","kind":"comment","references":"2799cec623715dd9d7845c1c09148964434dcb8054bebd82cbb899a50a505b89","summary":"People's and devices' views also drop `agent` when the comment's session row has no name or is gone, so those agent comments are keyed remote:<origin>#*owner too","tags":["security","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:17:29.308035Z","id":"acc6523336aa1c98d82d9bd2f263e215d3c54a157d27cd12b4f38bed3135cf28","body":{"detail":"Failure: the Clax app built from this branch connects to clax.dev (or any self-hosted Clax) whose server predates this branch. The app always calls POST /api/remotes with kind \"clax-app\" (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart addRemote), and start_sign_in adds client_kind to POST /api/hosted/device/code (public.rs:737-740). On main, crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs DeviceCodeBody is #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] with client_name alone (`git show main:crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs`, line 1016), so the remote answers 400 invalid_json; the core turns that into 502 remote_refused, and ConnectSheet._start (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart:158-166) shows 'Couldn’t start signing in to <host>. Try again.', which fails identically on every retry. Nothing tells the person the server is too old, and nothing in the repository orders the hosted deploy before the app's release (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md has no rollout section). Concern 24555b7b records the field skew at this function's old line range; this record is the user-visible failure. No test can catch it: every test runs the core against a public Clax built from the same tree (crates/clax-testkit/src/remotes.rs Public).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":730},"end":{"line":742},"content_hash":"91c34c744be7bd52a1a0570e23ed400a80e34c3d6218072110940b646f21273a"},"suggested_fix":"Map a 400 from /api/hosted/device/code when client_kind was sent to a distinct core error (e.g. 502 remote_too_old naming the origin) and have the connect sheet say '<host> needs an update before the Clax app can sign in'; record the deploy order (hosted before app) in the spec or release script; add a test against a stub remote whose device/code body denies unknown fields.","summary":"The Clax app cannot sign in to a hosted Clax running main's code: start_sign_in sends client_kind, which main's DeviceCodeBody refuses, and the app says only 'Try again'","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","compat","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:17:29.308162Z","id":"acac35af5c7385280e4d1cf7a977b502acf4cb7b69b34af57d0627b513593cb5","body":{"detail":"send() adds comments: false and forked_from to POST /api/artifacts for a new app copy (lines 1281-1287). main's clax_core::publish::PublishRequest is a plain #[derive(Deserialize)] without deny_unknown_fields (`git show main:crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs`, line 43), so an older remote silently ignores both and creates the copy with Comments on and no forked_from. The core reads only the artifact ID and version from the answer (lines 1313-1314), records the link, and reports success; the following bundle upload (PUT /api/artifacts/<raid>/versions/<n>/bundle, a route main does not have) then fails 404. The person is left with a published, commentable copy without a bundle, contrary to the decision that comments are off by default. Reachable whenever the core holds a token for an older remote: a daemon signed in without a kind (POST /api/artifacts/<aid>/push mode app is open to the owner from any client), a self-hosted instance not yet upgraded, or clax.dev rolled back.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1278},"end":{"line":1314},"content_hash":"64735dfe7041a7056e7f91e3cff51c95aa8a82aee9b4b3c8006405dbd37499eb"},"suggested_fix":"After a create in app mode, require the answer's artifact.comments to be false (this branch's create always answers it, routes/artifacts.rs create); when it is absent, delete the copy just made (or leave it unlinked) and refuse with a code naming the remote as too old. Alternatively probe once per remote for a route this branch adds (GET /api/hosted/apps) before the first app publish.","summary":"An app-mode publish to a hosted Clax that predates this branch makes a public copy with comments on and no lineage, and the core never checks","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","compat","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:17:29.308278Z","id":"88a32db065dff9025d4efb8cd45c60d362f38f9e124537b5043aa532e66bf512","body":{"detail":"Before this branch /a/{aid}/{*rest} served /a/<id>/get and /a/<id>/get/ as the shell for the file get or get/index.html. The two new routes match first, and get_page::page answers a non-app artifact 404 'This page isn’t an app yet.' (shell/get_page.rs not_an_app) and refuses agents 403. Publishing still accepts those paths (nothing in crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs reserves get), so existing links and in-page links such as href=\"get/\" (a 'Get started' section) break silently on upgrade, locally and on clax.dev. docs/contract.md (Get in Clax, line 1294) does not say the path shadows a file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":594},"end":{"line":595},"content_hash":"bbe46664df563297cae5b23357a8acff82adc6429dc8a03249c66624fd051ad4"},"suggested_fix":"Fall through to the artifact page when the artifact carries no bundle (or when its current version has a file at get or get/index.html), or refuse such paths at publish and document the reservation in docs/contract.md.","summary":"/a/<id>/get is now reserved on every daemon: a page with a root file named get, or a get/ folder's index, loses that address and shows 'This page isn’t an app yet'","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:19:00.470760Z","id":"710e1341abec3de319aa007b694d0749d6a8a232836bfd4188090cbb8c5e2f2e","body":{"detail":"The mechanics hold: crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:735-739 adds client_kind when kind is given; `git show main:crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs` lines 1015-1021 show DeviceCodeBody with #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] and client_name alone; a non-2xx non-401 answer maps to 502 remote_refused (public.rs:192-210); apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/connect_sheet.dart:161-166 shows 'Couldn’t start signing in to $_host. Try again.' for any code other than remote_exists/remote_unreachable. This branch's own server accepts the field (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1120-1128), so app and server built from the same tree work together. The failure needs a deployment skew (clax.dev or a self-hosted Clax older than the app), which scripts/release.sh:924-928 already prompts against by listing the clax.dev redeploy for releases with hosted changes, though it does not order it before an app release. No user hits this from the merge itself; it is a compatibility/rollout risk with a poor message, which fits concern (or a waiver with a recorded deploy order), not blocker.","kind":"comment","references":"acc6523336aa1c98d82d9bd2f263e215d3c54a157d27cd12b4f38bed3135cf28","summary":"downgraded: concern — the skew failure is real but arises only against a remote not yet upgraded, a rollout risk rather than a defect in the merged code","tags":["verified:downgraded","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:19:00.471131Z","id":"1139542f82630f77fd759cabf78996a4aa41854b3987e02df896cdb184b82873","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:1281-1286 sets body comments=false and forked_from for a new copy; 1313-1315 reads only remote_id(&res) and version.n. `git show main:crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs` lines 43-58: PublishRequest is #[derive(Clone, Debug, Deserialize, Default)] without deny_unknown_fields and has no comments or forked_from field, and main's routes/artifacts.rs create (line 444) parses the body into it, so both are dropped without error. `git show main:crates/clax-server/src/router.rs | grep bundle` finds no /api/artifacts/{aid}/versions/{n}/bundle route (this branch adds it at crates/clax-server/src/router.rs:129-132), so the following bundle upload 404s. Kind concern fits: it needs an older remote.","kind":"comment","references":"acac35af5c7385280e4d1cf7a977b502acf4cb7b69b34af57d0627b513593cb5","summary":"confirmed: app-mode create sends comments/forked_from that main's PublishRequest silently ignores, and the core reads only the ID and version back","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:19:00.471705Z","id":"43e45d520db101dcd3747b8b2482a9d8339f3609f6e8c285e678683e443ce1aa","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs:593-595 adds the two routes before /a/{aid}/{*rest} (line 604); on main (`git show main:crates/clax-server/src/router.rs` lines 523-527) those paths fell to shell::artifact_page. crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs:292-323 refuses agents, then answers not_an_app (line 212-218, 'This page isn’t an app yet.') whenever latest_app_bundle is None, never falling back to the artifact's file. `grep -n '\"get\"\\|reserved' crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs` finds nothing, so publishing a root file get or get/index.html is still accepted. docs/contract.md:1294-1300 (Get in Clax) does not mention that the path shadows a file. Kind concern fits.","kind":"comment","references":"88a32db065dff9025d4efb8cd45c60d362f38f9e124537b5043aa532e66bf512","summary":"confirmed: /a/<id>/get and /a/<id>/get/ now route to get_page::page ahead of the file catch-all, with no publish-side reservation or contract note","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
