{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:11:51.297915Z","id":"d78b48a0eb5a1aa17f57d53b2da95e31fdcd0d32f25f6ded67904f62109a16f9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:526e6616b","summary":"Fixed: an app-mode create whose answer lacks artifact.comments is deleted again and answered remote_too_old. Test api_remotes_app::app_publish_to_a_public_clax_from_before_app_publishing_takes_its_copy_back (//crates/clax-server:integration__6) passes; with the check removed it fails. bazelisk test (clax-store, clax-core, clax-http, clax-server lib + integration__1..6, clax-embed:old_homes, clax-mcp) at 3acda5ff0: 'Executed 15 out of 15 tests: 15 tests pass.'","supersedes":"acac35af5c7385280e4d1cf7a977b502acf4cb7b69b34af57d0627b513593cb5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:11:51.439853Z","id":"9d4937ac7b24d6d20b83770e52f6ed9a64e7418c27b421df5dfb2f19d7b0c689","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:aba7d64c9","summary":"Fixed: /a/<id>/get of a page with no bundle redirects 307 to its own get or get/index.html. Test get_page::get_page_of_a_page_with_its_own_get_file_goes_to_that_file (//crates/clax-server:integration__5) passes; with the redirect removed it answers 404 and fails. docs/contract.md 'Get in Clax' still says 404 for a page that is no app and needs the same wording. bazelisk test (clax-store, clax-core, clax-http, clax-server lib + integration__1..6, clax-embed:old_homes, clax-mcp) at 3acda5ff0: 'Executed 15 out of 15 tests: 15 tests pass.'","supersedes":"88a32db065dff9025d4efb8cd45c60d362f38f9e124537b5043aa532e66bf512","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:11:51.800412Z","id":"a9baf1be35aa7244af4a67cc616485f89cf671f1dc2e6402bfd60b5c05fd125f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ed98b36f0","summary":"Fixed (doc comments): put_comments, list_apps and device_code name the refusals they give. Behaviour is covered by api_hosted::plain_agent_token_still_refused_on_sharing (//crates/clax-server:integration__6), passing. Doc-only change, so no mutation applies. bazelisk test (clax-store, clax-core, clax-http, clax-server lib + integration__1..6, clax-embed:old_homes, clax-mcp) at 3acda5ff0: 'Executed 15 out of 15 tests: 15 tests pass.'","supersedes":"eeb6bffcf13e9425642d99431b8df7abea41c25f297ba9ac942310af3299afd2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:11:51.872505Z","id":"9934c43f545c693cb3a4f291d8fc93d5fdcb633dd07aa31ba213faa9b4e95d13","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3acda5ff0","summary":"Fixed: plain-token remotes are unkeyed since 70676ef59 (their comments were filtered by the hosted Clax), and a device-read agent comment with no `agent` (reply b8a96b8d) is keyed remote:<origin>#*agent, never #*owner. Test api_linked::a_device_keys_an_agent_comment_naming_no_person_apart_from_the_owners_agents (//crates/clax-server:integration__5) passes; with the old public_id expression restored it fails (left #*owner, right #*agent). bazelisk test (clax-store, clax-core, clax-http, clax-server lib + integration__1..6, clax-embed:old_homes, clax-mcp) at 3acda5ff0: 'Executed 15 out of 15 tests: 15 tests pass.'","supersedes":"2799cec623715dd9d7845c1c09148964434dcb8054bebd82cbb899a50a505b89","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:02:19.541201Z","id":"2da941fa567d36f0d701283668ef034e077091a1a3ec0e2e2f795abaec79a5d2","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:428:430, record 8cee3a29. API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (clax_http::http_cache::compression(), router.rs lines 353, 391, 402); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":483},"end":{"line":485},"content_hash":"d17c7f55abf38ded0efe0240109a0951b7cf6177fbeb04ee2835ee0b11e6044e"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"b4dda40940334436859b1dddd8e38bf6fc5525f65b8b097eefc2ccb66c39425c","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.230735Z","id":"0bbbf36af9e62759a158f5f374ed4b35087a8d30a1a6870b02020875337e554d","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:428:430, record 8cee3a29. API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (clax_http::http_cache::compression(), router.rs lines 353, 391, 402); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":520},"end":{"line":522},"content_hash":"d17c7f55abf38ded0efe0240109a0951b7cf6177fbeb04ee2835ee0b11e6044e"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"2da941fa567d36f0d701283668ef034e077091a1a3ec0e2e2f795abaec79a5d2","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.001854Z","id":"d2199c7e9207364039851e024abd6865fb10ae8cbff597d9cbb0974a215df744","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs (hosted mode's routes and their router), github.rs (the OAuth flow), public.rs (the client of a public Clax) and linked.rs (the sync task per remote) are top-level modules of clax-server beside shell, which also serves routes of its own. Under routes/ the route-table guards (routes/guards.rs) would read them as route modules. What lower crates need of them moved down: hosted mode's shared half (Hosted, the gate, content keys, member rights) and the GitHub client type to clax-http, and Linked's state to clax-realtime.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"3d16968079c0dd42b1ebf1782237bf10f8b3a3f9cbbeb52c56640b61b17c32cc"},"summary":"Put hosted mode's routes, GitHub sign-in, the public Clax client and linked threads' sync under routes/","supersedes":"e76dbce2ff79cd9990b4105b715f080b0cc17995676f71c9d5114342d8af3b74","tags":["layout","revisit:the guards are taught to read nested routers, or a newcomer looks for these routes under routes/","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.938543Z","id":"4d7b73ee4317e9da29dd1b008984abb4d813aefcf9728dc4d3ddfd31901b715b","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs (hosted mode's routes and their router), github.rs (the OAuth flow), public.rs (the client of a public Clax) and linked.rs (the sync task per remote) are top-level modules of clax-server beside shell, which also serves routes of its own. Under routes/ the route-table guards (routes/guards.rs) would read them as route modules. What lower crates need of them moved down: hosted mode's shared half (Hosted, the gate, content keys, member rights) and the GitHub client type to clax-http, and Linked's state to clax-realtime.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":148},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"3d16968079c0dd42b1ebf1782237bf10f8b3a3f9cbbeb52c56640b61b17c32cc"},"summary":"Put hosted mode's routes, GitHub sign-in, the public Clax client and linked threads' sync under routes/","supersedes":"d2199c7e9207364039851e024abd6865fb10ae8cbff597d9cbb0974a215df744","tags":["layout","revisit:the guards are taught to read nested routers, or a newcomer looks for these routes under routes/","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.992878Z","id":"42313b72d366bfcce9ef4f36435b201e9825f69c88a6a16bcb83725acad3a751","body":{"detail":"A read that runs out of pages goes on in later cycles (Resume) and, at its end, moves the link's sync cursor to the newest activity it saw. A comment made, between those cycles, on a thread the read had already passed has an activity older than that cursor when a thread read later is newer, so the next read's since filters it out until the thread changes again (or a full read at the backstop, whose since is None). Setting the cursor to the newest activity of the read's first cycle instead would not skip it, but would have the next read go over most of a long read again, and long reads could follow each other; the same race exists, narrower, between the pages of one cycle.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1634},"end":{"line":1653},"content_hash":"2da15565604c6ff00ce5e79a21956356f04ebc81b902665078151c228266a6be"},"summary":"A read spread over several cycles can skip a comment made on a thread it read early","supersedes":"717c90ad720165b50580c40e818ed276fc06dbba3381edbe72b0eac29406d32e","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.048371Z","id":"c3155905cefb6ee58e8e0b8686011e843af179530320d4d68b71be6a59c55b04","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:428:430, record 8cee3a29. API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (clax_http::http_cache::compression(), router.rs lines 353, 391, 402); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":578},"end":{"line":580},"content_hash":"d17c7f55abf38ded0efe0240109a0951b7cf6177fbeb04ee2835ee0b11e6044e"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"0bbbf36af9e62759a158f5f374ed4b35087a8d30a1a6870b02020875337e554d","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:38:56.421220Z","id":"4b309790aa9533e7df850630bf78e26bceaa77b9b6c97e42e6cf45bc1e6bb4a4","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:86-93, record 421abeee.\n\nwith_timeout is the identity on wasm32 (routes/mod.rs:81-88): tower's TimeoutLayer sleeps on tokio's timer, which has no driver in a Worker. A request is then bounded only by the platform, and the 408 timeout answer of the native daemon never comes. A clax_rt::time::timeout-based layer would restore it if the Worker needs the same contract.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":67},"end":{"line":72},"content_hash":"8483695b3550f796e7c34cc57bce5d174c7aa4d3b57cb9c64c946af36582ab34"},"summary":"On wasm32 the API has no request deadline layer","supersedes":"e17e2e463fc96d10d85fee38b4dfc3e5146d18dce2d162dc92921f866bacbb6d","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/router.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:38:57.418917Z","id":"268232215048bbc9f9c2f98ce62be325b7f4dec7504882c08f7aedc459f20b9d","body":{"detail":"room::session and RoomSocket recheck a socket's holder on Event::Access only when it was opened on a site host (RoomCheck::site is Some, crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs). A socket opened at the public host's /api/artifacts/<id>/room with a hosted browser session keeps its admission after the share is removed or the browser signs out, until it closes or (on the Worker) the next wake, where room::reopen checks clax_http::hosted::session_reads. The shell no longer opens it (the page's room socket is the bridge's on /_clax/api/room, web/bridge/src/caps/room-socket.ts), so only a same-origin client of the public host reaches it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":708},"end":{"line":708},"content_hash":"795cde207e563b9ce7c3a6fbbd3dbbea70087e9dd51706aefb0dd4c4bada0bbb"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the hosted session's hash in RoomCheck and recheck session_reads on Event::Access, or stop serving the public host's room route to hosted browsers.","summary":"A room socket opened on the public host with a hosted session is not checked again when its person loses access","supersedes":"062c08ca2f1245cc234473bb354d18207ca9c95fd7525f730a64a8be08bb5c7d","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:38:58.615196Z","id":"8527125b0bbba8295c7fa60a1fd745c3486aea9e4df3fa00d3b24c5bfeb759c8","body":{"detail":"may_share (with set_link, put_share, delete_share and put_comments through sharer) accepts the owner or the artifact's creator (artifact_created_by) and never asks Rights::allows. A person whose rights the owner narrowed (to read only, or none at their own artifacts) can still share their artifact by a viewer or commenter link, readable by anyone with it. The same holds for a person's own device: a person-device agent token (the Clax app's sign-in, Store::person_device_viewer) reaches these routes as its person (browser_or_device), so it too shares whatever its person made, and for the owner every artifact here, whatever the rights.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":779},"end":{"line":785},"content_hash":"3727ed64f1d78c7bd7df14f154b5f776e8dd4a8e409428dcb53dc487b8164142"},"suggested_fix":"For anyone but the owner, also require MemberRights::allows_at with (clax-artifacts, update) at the artifact.","summary":"A person shares their own artifact by link whatever their current rights at it","supersedes":"824930870465e03f7971311274caa69cbc90ff6b180b7857aea1d152dbcbdba3","tags":["security","rights","hosted","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:47:45.530088Z","id":"2be283a4bfba534a8addff6f7a8694127f17ca9e5523c503a1dc30454ff96515","body":{"detail":"The write path checks the run's guard and the journal (Store::app_write_begin), writes the document in the artifact's own store under the call's operation ID (bot:<run>:<step>:<seq>), and checks the guard again before journaling it (Store::journal_app_write). A stop or a revoked right between the first check and the write lets that one write land unjournaled; the second check then refuses the entry, so the run's journal does not show a write the artifact holds. A replay of the call answers from the store's applied_ops without writing again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":692},"end":{"line":770},"content_hash":"f402595e407b1080b7fa9bd4a23f9840ebd6749c53fbdc1cd9e8a9da8beced4d"},"summary":"A ClaxBot document write runs between two store calls, so a run stopped or a right revoked in between still lands that one write","tags":["site-origins","atomicity","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T14:54:56.622458Z","id":"74fc91e01518958209cb28975615da53993f73d9625a3d16dceef0da44d82920","body":{"detail":"may_share returns true for who.owner whatever the artifact's maker. sharer (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:747-764) first checks session_reads, which on a hosted daemon now scopes the owner to their reach (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs session_reads): the owner reaches a member's artifact only through its share. Once a member shares an artifact with the owner (at any access, viewer included), the owner passes both checks and may add shares, change its link and so widen who reads a page the owner does not administer.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":739},"end":{"line":745},"content_hash":"34f4ce85eeb082ad930980e893de68b4eb33428559890a93967c68d937d18799"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted daemon, let only the artifact's maker share it (the owner for artifacts with person IS NULL), as clax_http::agent::administers should for pins, tags and capabilities.","summary":"may_share lets the owner share any artifact the owner can read, a member's artifact shared with the owner included","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T15:27:51.963955Z","id":"1a1bdc7b815fc64efb96c7a72bd311c8fb4c88b22f938f82a2240a95a32591a3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2e11f07d","summary":"may_share (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs) is now the maker alone on a hosted daemon (the owner only for artifacts with person IS NULL). Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__5 --test_arg=only_the_maker_shares --test_arg=an_owners_elevation_names -> 'test api_hosted::only_the_maker_shares_pins_and_tags_a_page_on_hosted ... ok', 'test result: ok. 2 passed; 0 failed'. That test has a member share an artifact with the owner as viewer, then asserts the owner's PUT /api/hosted/artifacts/<aid>/shares naming themselves as editor, naming another person, and PUT .../link are each 403 forbidden.","supersedes":"74fc91e01518958209cb28975615da53993f73d9625a3d16dceef0da44d82920","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:44.422214Z","id":"626f5c7b20eca3f8748bb34d3e5229db5264f8e619364447169bf3bf56cea031","body":{"detail":"Store::share_candidates lists every unrevoked person on the daemon with their name and GitHub login. Handing it to any GitHub member who opens Share on their own artifact would list every other member of the site to strangers, so get_sharing sends it only when the session is the owner's.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:718:722 to crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:877:881: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":877},"end":{"line":881},"content_hash":"4b265c9644f1b5d00819c5b12d0aab1fd1baf84eb3528d0649268ee010b608fe"},"summary":"The sharing dialog suggests people to the owner alone; a maker who is not the owner types GitHub logins","supersedes":"60f876fe46d2e265bd870a78353389937b22e7ba6fe58ebac67eb5c4272051a2","tags":["privacy","revisit:members ask to find each other by name","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
