{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:06.338405Z","id":"b1230fac40d24c76060a9cde37309fc491d838ca3063172b05cb146f9900d9ec","body":{"detail":"may_share (with set_link, put_share, delete_share and put_comments through sharer) accepts the owner or the artifact's creator (artifact_created_by) and never asks Rights::allows. A person whose rights the owner narrowed (to read only, or none at their own artifacts) can still share their artifact by a viewer or commenter link, readable by anyone with it. The same holds for a person's own device: a person-device agent token (the Clax app's sign-in, Store::person_device_viewer) reaches these routes as its person (browser_or_device), so it too shares whatever its person made, and for the owner every artifact here, whatever the rights.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":762},"end":{"line":773},"content_hash":"797b3021464e2348c9f2d2f08a4a80ac9e37bb1d1cffb8732458841d2bdc7490"},"suggested_fix":"For anyone but the owner, also require MemberRights::allows_at with (clax-artifacts, update) at the artifact.","summary":"A person shares their own artifact by link whatever their current rights at it","supersedes":"824930870465e03f7971311274caa69cbc90ff6b180b7857aea1d152dbcbdba3","tags":["security","rights","hosted","review","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
